        <Document ID="D0F76F11-CEE9-483C-8DB6-BE5A5C182C65">
            <Title>Kleo in Heaven</Title>
            <Synopsis>Kleo rids the Elvises of possession, but is killed himself.
Kleo wakes in heaven and is not happy about it.  (Should be moved to the very rear of the book - after the end of the story)
</Synopsis>
            <Text>
Kleo in Heaven
10 Weeks after Bombing
“The demon meme left the bodies of your brethren as promised, but it took Master Kleo.” Silo explained to the High Elvis through a fog of tears and anguish.
“It has been rumoured he gave his life for the Elvi.” The High Elvis was devastated by the passing of the wisest of all the sages. 
“It is true, High Elvis. He gave up his life to save you all from ignorance and fear.”
“He will be remembered and he will be honoured.”
“He was honoured to have served you. We would be honoured to continue his work, to battle the certainty of faith.”
“You and Chilo will always have a home with the Elvi.” 
* * *
Kleo awoke to the vision splendid. Before him was beauty unlike anything he could have imagined, so stunning, so sublime, so…. “Oh, crap.” 
“Coming to see dad?” Jesus said. “He’s got a bit of explaining to do.”
“You know, you really do look like Caesare Borgia.”
“I know, it’s an amazing likeness. You will have to meet dear Caesare and his family, simply lovely people.”
“That sounds really good.” Kleo shook his head. The entry standards are set pretty low, thought Kleo, highly amused.</Text>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="278EDE85-2E98-459B-877D-C1B436880756">
            <Title>Summary</Title>
            <Text>Summary
Chapter One - Surf’s Up -2 billion years before the Dawkins
Describes a collision between two super-giant black holes.
I wanted a “tsunami” of gravity waves strike the earth, 2 billion years later, in a timely fashion that saves the day.
I probably won’t use it.

Chapter two - Vershlingbessern - 20 years before the Dawkins
The nation of Ulyssia (Large southern continent not un-like Australia) is invaded by a nation to the north.
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        
The Prime Minister of Ulyssia begs the President of the Union of Capitalist Atlantic States (UCAS), Dunnning Kruger, for military intervention. The President declines to help with ‘boots on the ground” because they are fighting the war against anti-semitism” in 10 theatres of war. Instead Kruger air-bursts 100 nukes over the invading troops and incinerates about 2 million of them. The invasion is defeated, but the land is glowing with radio-activity.
The UACS charges trillions of credits (or whatever they are - I don’t really name the currency) and pretty much bankrupts Ulyssia.Due to his incompetence, the Prime Minister is killed in an in-cabinet coup - his last words ‘et tu Brute’. 
All of the inhabitants of the western province of Western Ulyssia have to evacuate to the eastern ‘states’ creating a refugee problem. The locals take advantage of them and they are used pretty much as slaves.
The Western Province (with hardly anyone there) succeeds and call themselves the new country of Western Ulyssia.
The eastern part of the country decides to concentrate on manufacturing weapons and change the name of Ulyssia to the Primary Trade Dominion. They will sell weapons to anyone and also develop some nasty biological weapons.
Introduction to character Jamison Hardy - mega rich, but outwardly not a total arsehole. He appeared to try an protect the refugees from Western Ulyssia. His company manufactures weaponised viruses and were trying to make bio-weapons thata target specific genomes or even specific people.
A viral plague called “The viral cleansing” erupts in Ulyssia - no one knows what happened, but Jamison Hardy disappeared - presumed dead.
There are a bunch of descriptions that would be better coming from a character that the author, but I haven’t got to that yet.


Chapter 3 - Part one - Changing Brooms - 
14 Hours before the nightclub bombing - 9 months before the Dawkins
Introduction to Anthony “Cracker” Hardy (name will have to change as I think the name Cracker will not resonate with some readers)
He is cleaning an office and looking out the window at the the skyscrapers jutting upwards out of the “layer” (thick permanent layer of cloud/pollution floating about 200m above the sea level.)
As he looks out of the window, two hover-copts crash in mid-air and plummet to through the layer to the ground below. The layer opens  up around the burning wrecks and the layer burns for a short time before coalescing. Rich people do not travel on the ground - only by air and if they have to die to avoid mingling with the low-life’s on the ground, so be it.
Cracker point’s out the crash to the office workers, but none are interested enough to lookup and no-one would acknowledge the scum-bag cleaner in their midst, just shake their heads that a cleaner would have the effrontery to try to talk with them. 
Then moves into the office where a level 5 executive had committed suicide. He used a shotgun (not a particle pulse weapon!) and it was a real mess - brain stains. 
The new occupant of the office, Sarah Jacobson, arrives expecting the office to be ready. She is a stunning blonde. Cracker is a silly child in her presence,but manages to crack a (sort of) joke and gets the office ready for her. He explains he got the cleaning job through a contact in the police, Lieutenant Shakti.

Chapter 4 Lieutenant Shakti -People’s Hero 
9 months before the Dawkins
Introduction to Lieutenant Shakti - complete moron with no social skills. Born into a Level 5 home he wanted for nothing, but learned nothing instead. He shocked and embarrassed his well-to-do parents by applying to join the police (the public service!) and only just managed to stumble through training. There are some “back-story” examples of his abject stupidity.
Also introduction to his mother Eloise Shakti - super intelligent and ruthless. Managed to get from the lower levels to level 5 by sheer force of will. 
Narrative about his training in the police academy - how he was truely hopeless , but as a level 5 he could not be failed. The rest of upper level society would not have it. He finally showed some aptitude when he received media training. He was actually good at reading to camera (from auto-cue) and he was sent to take up a position in the “Public Affairs Bureau” - dealing with the media. 
Shakti also has a video streaming show known as Random Camera where the cops randomly select a house (of the lower class) and sets up cameras and listening devices. They then recorded everything in the house until someone committed a crime and then they would arrest. The most common crime is “Corporate Infidelity”, committed either by defaming a manager or breaching employer confidentiality. A very serious offence - doctrinal divergence of this magnitude was punishable by death.
Guilt is determined by a vote from the viewing audience. It is a very popular show as the upper classes hate the lows and love to see them suffer and die. Shakti introduces a show which is supposed to bring upper class fraudsters etc to book, but in actual fact the execution victim is always a low. (No level 5’s were harmed in the making of this show)
Voting by the audience is monitored by the PTD to ensure the upper classes don’t feel any compassion or deliver mercy. Indulging in compassion is moral weakness.
(A TV show that includes executions? What a trope!)
Chapter 5 - The Gyges Disc 
Return to Cracker leaving the Sarah’s office floor. 
He leaves via the “tradesman’s” elevator, but halfway down a level 5 dude (later it becomes clear this person is a company agent) gets in the lift and takes them back up to level 216 and gets out. 
He harrasses and threatens Sarah about the previous occupant of the office (Mr Lee) and wants to know where all of his property is. She stares him down and tells him the cleaner had just left with all of the rubbish. His mantra is “I am not human. I am the biological manifestation of the company’s will. In the name of stability I destabilize. In the name of order I deliver chaos. In the name of life I bring death.” 
The agent runs out to catch the cleaner.
Sarah reports the matter to security, but they are all watching Shakti’s show and she can’t get hold of them. She hacks the surveillance system, but is unable to locate the agent anywhere. There is no footage of him entering her office. She realises he must be a crazy company agent and she had sent him after the cleaner. 

At street level Cracker wanders out and trips over a man who had died on the sidewalk. Other pedstristrian walk around the body as if not to notice. The dead guy is dressed like an L.5. But has grubby fingers and dirty fingernails - definately not L.5. Cracker seaches the body and steals anything he can find.
Around the corner are two operational support officers who decide to pick up the body eventhough the agent has not re-appeared from the building. They approach the body and tell Cracker to piss off. The support officers pick up the body.
Cracker then leaves the area via the giant security gates that lead from the “Management District” to “The Pale”. He has a run in with a security guard who is trying to get him to upgrade his security ID from a tattoo to a brain implant. The Security Guard gets kickbacks from the brain implant mob for sending clients to them, but Cracker calls him on it and is finally let through.

Description of The Pale - dark horrible ghetto with a crime rate so unconscionably high the police never visit. Law enforcement is engage in shielding the rich from the poor, not protecting the poor from each other. “In the Primary Trade Dominion, egalitarians were those who ate eagle.” 
- - -
Sarah is concerned about the fact she sent an intelligence agent after Cracker and interrogates every data base trying to find out about him, but there is not much information - which is suspicious - entries had recently been deleted. She finds a couple of fines for drunk and disorderly (at the Stick it Inn) and that is about it.
She has to go to her promotional medical exam - which she passess. She is amused that the medical report notes she is not pregnant.

Chapter 6 - Pre-emtive Reciprocity 
The agent burst out of the building and onto the street, particle pistol in hand, but no-one is there.
No meat wagon - No Blank (a blank is a terminally ill person who is recruited for assassination on the promise their family would be taken care of after his/her death)
Worse still, he had misplaced a Gyges Disc. (Gyges disc - also called a cloak - is a small metal disc of unknown origin that makes the holder of the disc invisible to electronic surveillance.
His boss is not impressed - he has lost the disc, the blank and they don’t know where the operational support guys are.

Chapter 7 - The Blank
14 hours before the bombing
The blank was loaded onto the van by the operational support guys and taken to a morgue. They were diverted to the public morgue in an ultra-rich health and retreat area of the city and had spent a great deal of time getting through customs at the security gate. (There is an explanation as to why there is a public facility in an ultra rich area)
The blank, Emil Kalheri, was a level one labourer who had terminal testicular cancer and was recruited by the “Department of Pre-emptive Reciprocity and Proactive euthanasia”
He was recruited to assassinate Mr Lee and agreed after he was told Mr Lee was a paedophile. The agent, Agent Jones (his first name is Agent) arrives at the morgue and finally located the blank, but is not happy because the gyges disc is not with his property and he concludes the cleaner has the disc.
He then attempts to locate Cracker, but also finds there is nothing (or virtually nothing) on the cleaner. He thinks the cleaner might be from an unknown faction because only agents are afforded that degree of anonymity. 

Chapter 8 - Hot time in the ol’ town - 
4 hours before the bombing
(Sorry this chapter is trope-city)
Cracker gets home to find his live in partner is angry because he had not put them up for ‘allocation’ (marriage). She physically attacks him and with martial arts skills kicks the shit out of him and informs him she had place herself up for random allocation and had been allocated to James Marrin, BComm L.3.
She tell him she faked them all and then left. Cracker then arranges to go out with his mates for a celebratory drink at the “Stick it Inn” nightclub. It is an ‘open’ premises in that any level person could enter, but dress regulations were so strict only the rich could get in, unless, like Cracker, you have low connections everywhere.
His mates were waiting for him - Halo, Major, Abe. Halo was at the table staring at the crown trying to identify his net conquest. He was prolific in jagging women with a minimum of talk, if any. 
Halo id’s a woman and heads off to pick her up, but unusually he is back in double quick time, tail between his legs. The woman had rejected him outright. “Dykes, they’re all fucking dykes” he says to the boys at the table.
The woman who rejected him approaches the table - “Oh fuck, its her.” The woman is Sarah and she is looking for Cracker. Shortly after Halo spots another woman and he is gone. Major and Abe go to the bar and come back with drinks just before a bomb goes off obliterating the bar. Cracker and Sarah manage to crawl out of the rubble.
Cracker tells her they must leave. Anyone found near a terrorist incident will be arrested and interrogated, no matter who they are. They are smoldering and blackened with some serious cuts and bruises, but manage to hobble away. They get out of the immediate area, but realise their appearance will give them away. Sarah manages to hack (computer) their way into a public hygiene facility to clean up and wash the evidence of the explosion off them. Cracker tells her the water is tested for drugs, explosives, heavy metals &amp; contaminents and they must, somehow, block the drains. 
The drains are massive and Cracker chucks towels and chairs and anything he can get his hands on to block the drain. He is assists by a madman who jumps atop of the pile and starts calling for his “Comrads” to gather around. (He slips and gets stuck in the drain)
They each enter the facility - Cracker in the mens section, Sarah in the womens section. Sarah breaks into the control room of the facility and diverts the flow of the water (she does not know where) and also warms the water up 5 degrees. The shower are banks of cages, attached to the wall and stacked on top of one another. The top row get hot clean water, the lower cages just get what drips down from above.
They decide to go for the drink they did not get to have at the Stick It Inn and head for “The Quarter”. 

Chapter 9 - A Big Crush
When Cracker and Sarah get back to street level, there is a massive crowd . The Police have diverted everyone away from the bombing and have created a crush. 
Bit of back story of how Cracker knows Shakti. Cracker was on duty at a crush a few years earlier. A crowd of people had been crushed to death, but rigour-mortis had locked the crowd (mostly standing) together and they had to wedge the bodies apart to removed. They finally decided to use a big front end loader.
Cracker ducks off for a spew and finds Shakti vomiting on the ground. 
- - - 
Chapter 10 - Suicide Homicide
 - 2 Hours after the bombing
 (May be out of whack/time with the rest of the story)
Shakti is asleep and having a dream about his blonde dream woman. He is on a beach with pure white sand and crystal blue water. Something that no-one alive had ever seen. He ws walking along the beach holding the hand of dream-woman when she suddenly turns in to his mother and she tries to drag him off to college so he can become an accountant.
He is then awoken by a holo of the Commissioner of Police hovering over him. The Commissioner abuses him for his lackluster investigation into the Lee death. “Did I not send you to investigate a murder?” Shakti had written it off as a suicide. 
He is informed that there has been a coordinated terrorist incident where they had let off a bomb and then diverted the water away from the subsequent fires. Shakti think he is being given a terrorist incident to investigate but is disappointed when he is placed on clean-up duty at the public hygiene facility - level 5’s have had recyc diverted as drinking water!!!
Shakti, is hated by his peers and he know he will get no assistance from them. He turns to his only friend - Cracker.
- - -
Cracker and Sarah found themselves in the middle of a crush with no hope of getting out. Shakti contacts by mobile device and tells Cracker he needs him. Cracker tells him he can’t help, he is in a crush. Shakti tells him to standby he will be there shortly. Shakti turns up in a hover-copt and decends upon the crowd, who manage to make sufficent space. An armed police officer jumps out of the copter and gives Cracker and Sarah “forensic suits” and tells them to get in the copter. He turns to the crowd and shoots a number of the crown dead. Shakti tries asks if it was necessary to kill people he is told wounding them wrecks your shot to kill ratio - and ‘don’t worry I only shot white people so it wasn’t racist or anything.’  
They take off and Shakti briefs them on the job - terrorists have bombed a club and diverted the water away from the fire. Cracker and Sarah immediately afraid of being found out. 
They go back to the public hygiene facility - flooded with city workers unable to locate the drain. Cracker wades in. Sarah goes to the control room where city engineers and computer geeks are failing to restore the correct water flow. Sarah completes the task, but the blokes won’t give her any credit. 
Cracker unblocks the drain and manages to float the body of the guy who fell into the drain and got stuck. He floats him to the stairs and says to Shakti, “Here’s your terrorist.”
Shakti arranges a hover-copt to take them away telling them “Neither of you were here.”
 - - -

Chapter 11 - A Big Bang for the Big Bang
(At the time of the bombing - we have gone back a couple of hours)
Halo had seen the woman on the other side of the bar, just minutes before the explosion. He picks her up in double quick time and they are out the door. They kiss and are knocked over by the explosion. The go back to her house.
The woman, AVI, is an agent from the Department of Pre-emtive reciprocity and Proactive Euthenasia, who has been sent to place a bomb in the Stick it Inn (it is uncertain, but Cracker may have been the target).
They go back to her place - she plans to kill him, he plans to kill her. She is an assassin and he is a serial killer. (He is later identified as the “Nightclub Stalker/killer”)
The have sex and he kills her with a special knife/blade he had made. It is hollow in the middle so the blood spurts really high. However, because he stabbed her through the heart, the blood stopped pumping after a short time. He was not satiated and he goes out to find another victim.
He finds himself in the same crush as Cracker and Sarah. He stabs a few people and melts back into the crowd, but them he sights Cracker ex girlfriend, Angela. She is crying because her boyfriend suddenly disappeared and she thought he may have been trampled. Halo knows he must have stabbed him and he is greatly amused. He tells Angela they are is real trouble, but he might be able to get them off the street. He takes her back to Avi’s apartment. ‘He thought himself a simple man with simple needs – if he had a girl to fuck and stab, he was sweet.’ 

Chapter 12 - Dark Forces 
75 Minutes after the bombing - Immediately following the phone call with Shakti (Chapter 10)
The Commissioner of Police hangs up the phone on Shakti and makes a call to the CEO telling him Shakti fucked it up more than they had hoped. He called it suicide and went back to bed. No evidence collected.
The CEO is told the blank completed the job, made it look like suicide, but lost the gyges disc in the process. The blank had gone missing. The CEO wants the blank (Emil Kalheri) located as a priority.
The Commissioner was amoral and completely untrustworthy - making him a model public servant. He was a genius with malleable ethics. He contacts his most competent investigator,, Det Supt Hayley Lanning - she is one of the few honest cops on the force.
She is not happy about being put on a missing persons gig. She is in charge of the “Nightclub Killer” investigation and did not want to drop it to find a L1 labourer.

Chapter 13 - The Elvi (Pronounced El-Vye)
3 hours after the bombing
Sarah and Cracker can’t let the pilot know where they live so they get dropped off in the Quarter to see the Elvi.
- - - 
Cloning the Arts - Flashback 20years before the Dawkins. Dr Linus Grawling was a geneticist and music devotee. He hated modern music (rap) and spent years undertaking questionable (and criminal) research and scouring the globe to gather together the DNA of iconic musicians - raiding mausoleums, crypts, graves, ash filled urns. He cloned and cloned but found only one DNA strand that would readily lend itself to cloning. The DNA of a long lost singer - named Elvis. No-one knew his last name.
Cloned Elvis’ became pretty much mandatory for bars, restaurants, nightclubs etc. Every one of those type of businesses had one Elvis, some had nothing but Elvis employees. You had to keep them away from fatty food, guns, bizarre fashion and religion. For some reason the Elvi are especially susceptible to spiritual manipulation. If they were introduced to religion their warranty was void.
Vegas Show - The hover-copt dropped them in the quarter and they head to a bar. Elvis’s and Elvine’s are notoriously intolerant of the impolite and it is advisable to be as polite as possible when dealing with an Elvis. They were served by and Elvine and seated in a booth. From there they drink hard and watch the Elvi sing and dance in what was called a Vegas show.
Hangover - Cracker is suffering the worst effects of a night with the Elvi. Very hungover. ‘His blackened left eye was firmly closed shut and continually seeped a dilute blood-ooze that trickled over the collection of lumps, cuts, scratches and bruises that together contrived to construct something not too dissimilar to a face.’
Sarah is in his apartment, but they did not do the deed. He is below her station and she wishes to remain a virgin. 
While Cracker was asleep, Sarah had been surfing the link - the only news is the bombing and the coordinated diversion of water away from the fire. There was news that a terrorist had been caught by Lieutenant Shakti.
Sarah is concerned that Shakti can’t be trusted. Cracker tells her Shakti is not capable of self sacrifice, but he will never tell anyone a cleaner helped him - his mother would never let him live it down. 
She tells him about the visit at her office from a company agent. Cracker saw him on the elevator. She shows him the surveillance footage she had downloaded, there is no sign of the Agent, entering or leaving the office. Cracker has a look and notices that there is no trace of him leaving the office either - footage of him entering, but not leaving. Sarah did not notice this and he teases her about being smarter that her and then curls into a foetal position due to the excruciating hangover he is suffering through. He tells her where all the spoils from the previously day are and then crashes out. 
He wakes in fright, thinking that she had left, but she is still there and has looked at all the stuff he had knocked off the day before. Among the items are a wallet with id in the name of Emil Kalheri and a shiny silver disc the size of a thumbnail and a general access chip - will open any electronic-locked door in the dominion until expiration.
Sarah does not know what the disc is, but she can tell it is some sophisticate technology that the PTD will want back. 
Sarah also has uncovered information about Emil Kaheri - according to PTD records, Emil Kalheri died of testicular cancer quietly at his home the previous day - but Cracker had seen his body at the foot of Sarah’s building. Kalehri had no permit to enter the business district. They wonder how he got in and why was he there?
They discuss why the Commissioner thought the Lee suicide was murder. They also figure that the Commissioner knew Shakti would fuck up the investigation.
She resolves to contact a colleague/sort of friend (Johnny) in the computer hardware field. Arranges to meet the Johnny at the Memphis Mafia Bar and Grill. Johnny is not keen to go to street level - he had never been there before and heard the scumbags who live there cover the ground with mud. Cracker takes an instant dislike to Johnny (even before they meet) and calls him “The Johnny”. Sarah tells Cracker she has to meet Johnny on her own. She trusts him as much as anyone, which is to say not at all. “A friend is someone who will shit on you sometime in the future, generally the near future.
- - - 
Chapter 14 - Dr Logan
The day after the bombing - 9 months before the Dawkins

 Detective Supt Lanning took no time in locating Emil Kalheri at the public morgue in the Health Zone. She was greeted by a pretty young blonde pathologist in pig tails, Dr Kathy Logan L.5. She is bright and bubbly, always giggling and laughing.
Records show the body is already okay to be collected - the fee already paid by an anonymous benefactor - there are no records indicating who paid. Dr Logan asks what is all the interest in this particular body? She explains ‘spooks’ had visited the day before, wanting to know where the deceased’s property was.
Detective Lanning examines the body and identified a minor fresh blemish, about the size of a thumbnail on the inside of his right thigh. Dr Logan takes a sample of the blemished area. Dr Logan tells Detective Lanning that the deceased had a ingested a huge amount of the stimulant AMT.
 - - -
Chapter 15 - Death a la carte
Day after the Bombing 
Introduction to the Department of Pre-Emptive Reciprocity and Pro-active Euthanasia and Damien Hardman.
Just promoted to executive level Damien Hardman hates his new office. The floor of the building was smack in the middle of the layer and he could not see anything out his window. He was also having trouble getting hold of Agent Avi. They had tried every method of raising her, even rattling her brain implant, but they could not raise her. She had planted the device in the nightclub and then there was an immediate attack on the water supply. He she managed to do both?
Satellite tracking showed her to be at her home address and Damien decides to go an visit himself.
He finds the body of Avi and some unknown woman. He calls a santising team to take care of the bodies. They are thrown into a furnace. Avi and the unknown woman never existed.
He is then called to see the Director on the top floor of his building. He explains that Avi had placed the device as directed, but there had been an attack on the water supply. The director orders Avi;s contract terminated - Damien tells him he has already terminated her - wrapped and roasted. The Director is pleased.
Damien also tells him Shakti had fixed the attack on the water supply - but there were two other unknown people with him. The Director orders that these persons be identified, not interrogated or terminated.
 - - -
Damien leaves the office. The Director is contacted by the CEO who asks how such an easy job could go so badly. They don’t even know it the target (a cleaner) was among the dead. The only two who knew the identiy of the target is the Director and the CEO. To keep the secret, the CEO decides to terminate the Director. He picked up a small device and pressed the button - shortly after the Director’s Office manager entered, drew a particle pistol and killed the director before training the weapon on himself.

 - - -

Damien Gets a promotion - The CEO promotes the newly promoted Damien to Director. It amused him - the other directors will be shitting themselves.
Shakti’s chance to shine - The CEO contacts the Commissioner of Police and arranges for Shakti to investigate the Director’s murder. The CEO says Shakti has the precise skill set required.
CSI by remote control - Shakti arranges for Cracker to help him examine the crime scene. Wearing an ear-piece and a pair of video glasses,Shakti is “coached” by Cracker through the crime scene. Shakti shocks everyone by acting like a professional. 
 - - -
 Chapter 16 - Private Contractor
3 Days after the bombing.
Det Supt Lanning goes to interview the family of the missing person Emil Kalheri to get some background and sus-out whether the family was implicated. She finds the wife and two daughters murdered in the house - shot in an obvious execution. 
Back at the office she calls Dr Logan at the morgue and is told the body had 
 been collected by his wife that morning.Knowing the wife was dead that morning meant the body had been snatched. She also reports that the records had been tampered with - information she had entered and seen on the system had suddenly disappeared. Her IT guys had taken a look and could not find any evidence of hacking - too sophisticated for low grade techs.
Det Lanning promises to get an expert to assist in investigating the hack - She sees the Commissioner. Tells him she has managed to lose the missing person. (Doh!). Gets permission to hire a contractor who is an expert in cyber security - she argues the police employees are not good enough (but she just doesn’t trust them - corrupt and lazy.) He agrees, but stipulates the contractor must be prepared to go out into to the field on operational duty. (He was hoping the contractor would get killed so he didn’t have to pay out the contract.)
THE FOLLOWING IS HIDDEN SOMEWHERE - CAN’T FIND IT! I THINK THIS IS WHERE THE TIMING OF THINGS GETS OUT OF WHACK. THE NEXT CHAPTER GOES BACK A LITTLE IN TIME.
Det Lanning arranges a meeting with the Director of Cyber Security for the PTD. She is sent to and office to interview the candidate. The candidate is Sarah Jacabson PhD L5 - who shits herself when Lanning ID’s herself as a cop - she thinks she is going to be arrested in connection with the terrorist bombing and hack on the water supply.
She is surprised and a little insulted to be offered a contract in the public sector but the money is good and she signs up.
Chapter 17 - Sages of the Travelator
A day after the bombing
Sarah meeting her friend Johnny in the Memphis Mafia Bar and Grill. He is an arrogant Level 5 compter hardware specialist (or whatever they are called) She shows him the disc (carried in a mini-faraday cage) and although he had not seen one before he thinks it is a “Gyges Disc”. Allegedly runs on gravity waves and effects electronic surveillance making a person in possession of the disc invisible to surveillance.
He knows it is seriously high tech and thinks, since it is effected by changes in gravity, spinning might render it inert. He reckons he can jerry-rig a cocktail blender and orders the waitress, Elvine (female Elvis) to get him a blender. He is rude and arrogant and calls her a mobile drink dispenser. When she returns she smashes the glass blender over Johny head, leaving a nasty gash and knocking him out. Elvine leaves and speaks to a bouncer and it looks like the bouncer is being sent to deliver the expected beating, but Cracker turns up and manages to negotiate a safe passage out. In her haste Sarah sticks the disc in her bra.
They can’t take The Johnny to a local medical centre (if there is one) but they also can’t drag him across town to a medical centre. It is not forbidden, but it is impolitic for “Level 5’s” to be slumming it in the quarter - mixing with the working class. They decide to take him to Cracker’s slum. Johnny is still knocked out and they can’t drag him all the way so they decide to take a chance on “The Travelator” A massive 37km circle of train/tram carriages that at walking pace constantly circles some of the shittiest places in all of the PTD. It was supposed to be a cheap mode of travel for the lows, but it immediately turned into a giant mobile brothel/crackhouse and was very dangerous. There are a few safe carriages, but you have to take your chances. You jump on the moving carriage see what happens. 
They jump on and find three weirdo Druid types, Kleobulous, Silo &amp; Chilo, who welcome them give them some wine. Kleo tells them of the Dawkins, Scence and reason and the elegance of evolution. They quote parts of the “God Delusion” as if it is scripture and name Karl Sagan as a prophet. Every time there is a direct quote they say “Praise the Dawkins” or “So say the Chronicles of the Dawkins” (So I am sort of referencing it as the work of Richard Dawkins.)
He talks of Charles Darwin as “The One-before-the-one”, Dawkins as “The One” and the prophet to come - “The-one-after-the-one”. He tells of his belief that evolution will produce the person that will end the inequalities and appalling human suffering in the PTD. Theythen have to lock-down the carriage as they pass through the worst part of town. (Praise be to The Dawkins).
Chapter 18 - Viral
20 Years before The Dawkins 
Mega Rich Industrialist Jamison Hardy gets a message from his Head Microbiologist claiming he has made a remarkable discovery. By combining tardigrade DNA with other “super organisms” they created a virus that is a literal panacea. A world without disease.
- - -
Chapter 19 - Random Camera
Trope city!!
It is an episode of Shakti’s Random Camera complete with execution of a working class stiff. The video is a fraud but Shakti had to get ratings up and executions really rate.
There are also muscle men, dwarves and hostesses in bikinis.
My eyes roll too.
There is no reason to keep this bit, but he will still have a show on the link, but there will be no need to show it.
Chapter 20 - The Dawkins
On the travelator they are locked in as they travel through the Pale.Kleo tells them more of the Dawkins, religion, the notion of certainty (there is none) the comfort of ritual and evolution/science and reason. 
Also the back story of how the PTD came into being, the story of President Dunning Kruger and how the PTD came into being. He also speaks of the “Viral clensing” that killed off half of the PTD and took Jamison Hardy.
 They are attacked by some sort of criminal gang. They break in through the roof and a the carriage is filled with smoke, Sarah gets knocked down, a blow to the stomach, but recovers quickly. Shortly after they are move out of the Pale and the criminals apparently retreat, but it is a little uncertain as to what happened because of the smoke and debris that fell into their eyes.
He explains that they use religious ritual to spread the word of the Dawkins. He tells Sarah she will bear witness to it all.” (Praise be to the Dawkins)
Chapter 21 - The Johnny
They manage to get “The Johnny” back to Crackers and put him to bed. He is half conscious and whinges about the bed and demands clean sheets. Cracker is shitty as he has to break out the sheets he had stolen for a Christmas present. 
Cracker and Sarah are having a chat about the events of the day and she says, I had forgotten why we went out. Then she realises the disc is still in her bra. She rushes off to the bathroom and then freaks as the disc had commenced to bury itself in her breast, a thin layer of skin already over the top. She can’t budged it and begrudgingly has to call Cracker for help  He pops into the bathroom and she shows him the problem. They try to pop it like a giant zit, but it won’t budge. They decide it will have to be cut out and Cracker has to do the cutting. He does a good job, but it still won’t budge and suddenly the sight of breast got the better of him and he latches on and sucks it out. As they are finish the task The Johny appears at the door. He takes some convincing there was nothing sexual involved. 
Johnny has another look at the dics and sees that it has biological components saturated in synthetic DNA. He hypothesizes that some of that DNA may have passed into Sarah’s blood stream. 
Spoiler - Sarah has the panacea virus. It has passed onto the Gyges Disc and infected its synthetic DNA. The implication, of course, being that the nature of the disc may have changed. When Cracker sucked out the disc he was also infected with the virus (I think it will be the “Hybrid T Virus”??).
Chapter 22 - Tit Virus
Cracker wakes up feeling great. Fantastic. He looks in the mirror and sees that his wounds from the bombing are miraculously healed. Sarah freaks and knows that she has given him the virus, but she blames the “miracle” on the synthetic DNA in the disc. She tells him not to have sex. Not much of a problem for him.
Chapter 23 - Infected Disc

The next morning at Cracker’s The Johnny finishes off examining the disc. He notes the tendrils of the disc are not interested in him, but are keen to dig into Sarah and Cracker. Cracker wonders if he is going to turn into a Cyborg and calls Sarah “robo-tit”. 
To avoid any possibility of the disc sinking into Sarah or Cracker they decide The Johnny should keep the disc, but just to store it.
Cracker and Sarah decide that they have to seek some medical attention - there was no telling what the synthetic DNA might do to them. Problem being any anomalous readings would be reported. Cracker says he knows someone and they make loose plans. 
She has the new contract to start and she won’t be available for a week or so. ( This part is out of whack in time - she it not offered the contract for a couple of days!!! Whoops. Shouldn’t be too hard to fix. I will just say she won’t be available for a week - meetings and such) 
Cracker notes he will have to go to a few funerals that week anyway. (It’s only two days after the bombing). As she leaves he cries, she thinks its because of his dead friends from the bombing. A death of a couple of friends is nothing compared to being denied her presence. (They didn’t make it by the way - except Halo)
Chapter 24 - Panacea
20 years before the bombing
 
Jamson Hardy visits the the lab where the Panacea virus was created. He meets with the head micro biologist who looks 20 years younger than he did the last time Hardy saw him. He explains this virus seems to operate on the human biological system so as to maximise the efficiency of every system. It kills off human pathogens and may extend life indefinitely. It is spread through blood, semen 
Hardy is not happy about killing off the pharacuetical and cosmetics industries and decides to seal them in until he can make a decision. Before he leaves he asks to be innoculated - he gets a needle but we later (much later) find out it is a placebo.
Chapter 25 - The Big Sleep
The scientists at the lab have a meeting. They are were hoping Hardy would see the virus as the breakthrough that it is, but were prepared for a lockdown. They knew he would make the right decision, so a few days in lockdown was no big deal. They had also prepared for a long incarceration and had planned to send packages, with the virus, to their families. Only one of the packages was sent - that of the head biologist. He sent it to his fiance and her two daughter.
Explanation of how the virus was manufactured.
They are all infected and look great. Eg. The buck toothed woman now had straight teeth. 

Chapter 25 - Unexpected Expecting
8 to 10 days after the bombing
Cracker arranges to meet Sarah at the rear of the public mortuary and to meet his friend Dr Kathy Logan. She loves patching - patches with all sorts of drugs that can be programmed to come on or stop for periods of lucidity, which allowed her to patch all of the time.in 
She examines both of them and they are in perfect health, but there is a anomaly in Sarah’s results. She is pregnant.
Chapter 26 - Paternal Mystery
Sarah thinks Cracker must have raped her but he had only known her a week. Her medical report for her new promotion had specifically noted she was not pregnant earlier that week, but Dr Logan says the chemical produced (I name it) when the egg is fertilised is release 5 days after fertilisation and scans will show cell reproduction after 7 to 10 days. Cracker said it must be The Johnny.
Dr Logan breaks out the DNA sequencer and gets a sample of the child’s DNA. The results are that Cracker is not the father and Sarah is not the mother. 
Chapter 27 - A Deeper Mystery
Dr Logan says that there are many people in the world wide data base that share some of the DNA with the child and she may be able to cobble together a list of relatives. She notes that as she searches the data base the further she goes back in time she find relatives that are genetically closer, not further apart.
Chapter 27 - A good time to patch up
Dr Logan reports she finally worked out the genetic line and there is a precise match with a long deceased man named Richard Dawkins. She notes that the cloning is perfect, zero copying errors. - (Hybrid T virus made it perfect - the actual instrument that impregnated her was very hit and miss and made more mutants than near perfect copies) There are also “added sequences”.
They realise Kleo and crew are involved but haven’t worked out how. Sarah is really pissed off and leaves. Cracker and Dr Logan go out patching.
Chapter 28 - Elvi Rising
Sarah had dropped off the radar and Cracker was in mysery. He decides to go out on the piss, by himself (always a good idea) and starts up a conversation with a few Elvis’s who are scabbing free drinks after a set on stage. Cracker gets very drunk and tells them about Sarah and the one-after-the-one and evolution and of course, The Dawkins.
The Elvi are very susceptible to memes and pick this up and run with it. They writes songs about evolution “Evolve Me Tender” &amp; environmental issues“Burning Coal”. They brain dumped anything they could find about the Dawkins, science and reason, evolution. The songs are No1 hits world wide and the Elvi were able to share the profits as a single performer, but sales were so huge they had a vast wad to invest (in the PTD). They’re followers were legion and were called “Dawks” which were a virtual army of willing helpers who plaster “The-one-after-the-one” is coming posters all over the PTD. Everywhere, making buildings look like they were paper-maiche.
The Moral compliance directorate now take notice of the Elvi. They were alarmed that the the Elvi were spreading Religious propaganda with all the talk about “The-one-after-the-one” they are recognised as a direct threat to the PTD. The CEO decides the Elvi have to be wiped off the face of the earth. He recruits Damien Hardman to help.
Chapter 29 - The High Elvis
The rapid speed of their sucess necessitated the Elvi to organise themselves as a community. They vote Elvis 457 as “The High Elvis” (Their was debate as to whether he should be called “The King”, but they all reckon they are “The King” so it would have been controversial.) 
He gives an inauguration speech - all of the words are lines from Elvis Presley songs cobbled together to make an almost coherent speech. There is much praise for The Dawkins. He sings a song (not an Elvis Song) but a song/peom I wrote from “The God Delusion” called “Most Never Stirred”. 
 Most have Never Stirred
We are going to die
That is what we must face
We are the lucky ones
Most never join the race.
Never will they perish
Never to falter and fall
Owning no life to cherish
They were never born at all.
The number of human beings
Who could be here in my place,
Outnumber all the sand grains
On the Sahara’s sandy face.
Untold unborn poets rhyming better than Keats
Countless bright minds Newton could not resist
The set of potential people and their possible feats
Exceeds the set of human beings that ever will exist.
In the teeth of these odds stupefying
You and I living banal and trite
Are the privileged, there is no denying
Winning a grand lottery to breathe air here tonight.
How dare we find ourselves whining,
At the prospect of being interred
Returning to the prior state
From which most have never stirred.
There is a bit of a ruckus in the crowd with a number of Elvis’s on the ground having fits. They have ear phones in and when someone listened in he is horrified and calls out,, “Gospel Music!” and vomits and stumbles off. The crowd panics and crash into each other, climbing and clambering to get away. as the fitting Elvi starts calling out ‘Praise be to Jesus!’
They are quarantined and an investigation shows they were suffering from an extreme case of “Evangelism” had been listening to old music of the black dics. They stumble across some hymns. It started out innocent, a small choir but then they started holding while masses and engaged in sexual abstinence. 
The HIgh Elvis isn’t happy that one of the first things he has to do as the leader was to censor Gospel music.
Chapter 30 - Majority Report
20 years before the explosion
Jamison Hardy decides calls together a team of experts to his conference room on the top floor of Hardy Tower One. There is a massive glass dome over the room that refracts and bends the light in weird ways. The dome filters out all sorts of nasty radiation and if not there, the occupants of the room would be cooked. (In Cracker’s time this massive conference room has been converted into the world’s most expensive restaurant “Gravity Well.”)
He tells them he wants to know the effect upon the economy if a cure for all diseases were discovered. He locks them in the room and leaves by approaching what appears to be a solid polished stone wall, but as he approached a part of the wall shimmers of coalesces into a door which opens automatically. He walked through and the door shimmers back into stone.
Later that day the group makes a report that concludes - ““The miracle drug, if it exists or ever comes into existence, must be destroyed. All research must be destroyed and all related research staff must be eliminated.”
He orders the dome opened so the team is fried by the radiation. He then orders the labs (underground) be secured by pouring concrete, locking everyone in forever.
Chapter 31 - Viral Lockdown
20 years before the explosion
The concrete is poured but one of the labs collapses under the weight of the concrete. They pour more over the top, but a big air bubble had been released.
There is a pandemic that they could not fight because all theh best micro-biologists wer buried under 10m of concrete, so they had to recall a fugitive Dr Linus Grawling. He was on the runn because of his shocking human cloning fuck ups. He was recalled from the University of Memphis where he had been continuing his research.
When he came back he worked out that the virus was programmed to target a certain genome that was found in about 20 - 30 percent of the population. There was nothing he could do to save them, but he was able to identify who was going to die.
After the pandemic Jamison Hardy is not seen again.
Chapter 32 - Fireworm
Sarah sets up a little cyber-inivestigative team that sets to work trying to discover the source of the hacks. After some considerable time they discover a “Sleeping fireworm” program that was installed as a part of the original program. It moves and hides and when in operation they system cannot recognise it as a “hack”.
They discover that Cracker’s details were deleted by the program. There is a pattern of people disappearing after their details are erased and they figure Cracker is next. Sarah pretends not to know Cracker.
Det Lanning decides to grab Cracker and put him in protective custody. The Commissioner has bugs in their office and hears the plans. He contacts his secretary and says “Get me Shakti.”
Genesis of Genocide - Agent Jones gets dragged into the Director’s office and he gets a dressing down for losing the Gyges Disc and he is really pissed off that he killed the Kalheri family without authorisation. He is ordered to interrogate the “Operational Support Guys” (the guys that took the body to the morgue).
Just a few questions - Agent Jones tortures the operational support guys and they manage to remember the cleaner had “Cracker Jack Cleaners” on his overalls. Agent Jones torutres them to death because they are witnesses to his incompetence. His career being more important that their lousy lives.
An afternoon at Cracker’s - Sarah and Hayley go to Cracker’s but Agent Jones is already there torturing him, trying to find out where the disc is. Cracker plays for time and insults the agent &amp; fucks around. Because Cracker has the virus, Agent Jones has difficulty injuring or hurting Cracker even when he smashes him in the face with the butt of a gun. 
Sarah and Det Lanning enter and Sarah recognises Agentn Jones as the man who had entered her office and harrassed her. She over-powers him. He is hostile and makes all sorts of threats and laughs at Det Lanning when she tell him she is a cop - he thinks they are nothing but street sweepers. Det Lanning scares the shit out of him by aiming a pistol at his dead and then saying “BANG!” He has a Gyges Disc and Det Lanning takes it as evidence. He says don’t spin them unless you want to create a gravity well. She decides to shoot him, but at the last second he tells her the new Director of Pre-emptive Reciprocity and Pro-active Euthenasia is planning to dig up the Jamison Hardy bio-labs - he did not know why.
Agent Jones is recruited as an informant for the police and before they let him go, Sarah places a trace/intercept on his phone &amp; linked it to his brain implant (sort of a comms device) - if he does the wrong thing they will rattle his brain to pudding.He agrees to report to her daily.
Chapter 33 - I think you got me
Arrest - Sarah and Hayley Lanning leave Cracker’s house, Shakti and a massive arrest team arrive to arrest Cracker for the Nightclub Stalker murders. (Hayley had been in charge of this matter until she was alocated the missing person gig.) Hayley is shocked as she knows the investigation back to front and no one had been identified. Shakti tells her the Commissioner told him to arrest Cracker.
When Shakti sees Sarah he is is deep shock as she is the woman he dreamed of. (of whom she dreamed?) 
Cracker is arrested for murder - the commissioner has set him up. There is no compelling evidence, but it doesn’t matter becasue the Commissioner has arranged for Cracker to be killed in custody. A promotion for the person who kills him.

Co-opted Allocation
Shakti ducks off to contact his mother and tells her he has one for the list - Sarah Jacobson PhD, L.5.
Alibi Interview
At the police station/complex Hayley decides to assist Shakti with the interview of Cracker. (The Commissioner has listening devices in the interview rooms and can hear everything.
The murders have been committed by someone with a weapon that leaves a diamond shaped wound, so it is easy to connect the murders. One of the murder victims is his ex-girlfriends fiance who was murdered in the crush on the night of the bombing. She she decides to start questioning him about that murder (he at least has some connection to the deceased)
When interviewing Cracker tells them that on the night of the murder he says that a there are two people that can account for his whereabouts. He was with Shakti and Sarah Jacobson helping to clean up the public hygeine facility. Sarah is really shocked to find out Cracker knows Sarah and Shakti as well. She calls Sarah into the interview room and ensures she has the second Gyges Disc they took from Agent Jones so that know one can listen in.
She sends Shakti away to do some busy work and says to Sarah and Cracker “Now you two are going to tell me everything.”
Confession
Cracker and Sarah tell her everything (we return to the conversation at the end with Hayley saying “All that happened in a couple of days?” She knows that they didn’t set the bomb, but were thie idiots that redirected the water.
Hayley ponders why the Commissioner sent Shakti to arrest Cracker with no evidence and then she works out the once he was placed in the care of the custody officers, Cracker would be killed. They decide they have to sneak him out and their plan is to take Cracker to a apartment Sarah purchased (She bought the house of Mr Lee - murder victim - at a bargain basement price).
They try to get out but manage to walk into an ambush - firing squad. 
A Shot out of the Blue
Sarah shoots Cracker in the chest (high and to the right) and says the Hayley is going to get the promotion. The Sgt in charge of the firing squad is impressed and plugs him a couple of more times in the stomach, but when he goes to shoot him in the head Sarah knocks him flying - “I want him indentifiable.”
They arrange for a Coronial wagon to take Cracker to the morgue - where Dr Kathy Logan works. When they get there Dr Logan unzips the body bag (gets stuck around his groin and she jiggles it) certifies death and the wagon drives away. Cracker is not dead, the virus has protected him and commenced fast-healing. Dr Logan is buzzing on MDMA and hugs and kisses Cracker (&amp; gets the virus).
Dr Logan shows them the progress she has made with DNA of the child. She triggers a hologram to show two floating DNA helixes. One of Richard Dawkins and the other of the cloned child. When layed over one another the DNA is identical except for added pieces of synthetic DNA. She figured the synthtetic DNA was frommilitary hardware and expended all her favours to find out that the DNA is from a quantum bio-processor - that particular snipped of code is specifically related to data compression and storage. They then discuss what the effects of synthetic DNA would have on the developing child. No-one knows, but Kathy thinks that the child may have an almost unlimited capacity to store data. Discussion about termination if the child is a mutant. They palce a scanning patch on her stomach - reports all activity to DR Logan in real time.
Killer Show
Shakti’s show for that evening takes credit for the killing of the dreaded Nightclub Vampire and show endless replays of Sarah and the Sgt shooting Cracker.
At home, watching the showm Haloren Smythe Director, L.6. Says “What the fuck?” He was not happy that Cracker had been given the credit for the murders he had committed. He grabs a kit bag and heads for the door “Time for a fucking Crime spree.” 
Extra DNA
Cracker was healing nicely and now that he was officially dead he could leave his old, life behind him. He did not think he would become rich, but he was hoping he might jump a level or two. After all, he is the decendant of a dead rich cunt or is it rich dead cunt? (When he spoke with Kleoboulos in the travelator he was told he was a decendant of Jamison Hardy.)
Hayley claims the promotion for killing Cracker. Now Detective Chief Superintendent Hayley Lanning. 
Cracker and Sarah leaving the morgue, but Sarah want to confront the Sages for the unwanted pregnancy.
Chapter 34 - The allocation of Richard’s mother
The God Infusion 
The High Elvis sends a delegation of 8 Elvi to seek out the Sages in relation to the Elvi that are possessed by the Jesus. They are all martial arts experts - Karate Elvis, Tai Kwon Do Elvis etc and finally find the correct carriage.
The sages are surpirsed the Elvi are clued up about the Dawkins and they agree to go back to the Quarter to help with the possessed Elvi. Kleo is told of “The Great Teacher” (Cracker) and the Holy Mother (Sarah) rumoured to be carrying the-one-after-the-one. The Elvi then tell them 5 E;lvi had succumbed to the infection of religion and the promise of certainty. (Certainty? The most delusional state of mind.) The Sages go with 4 of the Elvi to the quarter to see if they can help with the Jesus possession. 4 remain to guard their keep. When he arrives at the Quater Kleo give a speech a about science and reason and how it shines a path to the truth - butr reminds them there is not ultimate truth. He then gives more background on the formation of the PTD. 
Exorcism 
The infected Elvis’s become wild and agitated when confronted with rational arguement. 
They go to conduct an exorcism on the infected Elvi who think they are going to heaven. Kleo aregues they are not born of water (woman) and cannot get to heaven. They are born of syringe and petri dish. A theological debate breaks out with Kleo using the arguements laid out in “The God Delusion” He is quoting “The Chronicles of the Dawkins” There is also reference to the Hartle-Hawking theory of the formation of the universe.
There is debate as to what to do with these Elvi - they are a danger to the rest of the Elvi nation.
Jesus takes and Elvis
They try all sorts of therapies on the Elvi but nothing seems to work. 
Kleo speaks to possessed Elvis 1 who claims to be Jesus. Kleo hits him with all of the arguements in “The God Delusion” about God (the father) sending God (the Son) to Earth on a pointless suicide mission. Instead of holy water, Kleo sprays him with heavy water - it burns the Elvis (only because it was hot). The eorcism is a direct parallel with the exorcism scene in the “Exorcist.”
He then says Your father had you hideously tortured and executed for a symbolic sin, committed by a person who never existed? Barking Mad! 
The Elvis then grabs hold of Kleo and they both drop to the floor. The Elvis kind of wakes up and says “What happened.” Kleo is dead.
Kleo in heaven
All of the Elvis’s are now cured of the possession. 
Kleo wakes up to the vision splendid. Jesus walks up and says your coming with me to see Dad. Kleo realises he is in Heaven and says “Oh, Crap!”
Elvis of the Travelator
Sarah and Cracker arrive to confront the sages but find only 4 Elvi in the carriage. The Elvi drop the their knees when they see The Great Teacher and the Holy mother. They are all excited about the prospect of the birth of the one-after-the-one. She tells them she does not even know if she is going to full term. The Elvis’s are horrified. They need the one-after-the-one to protect the Elvi from being infected by religion and they cannot be denied him. The Elvi are crying and beg her not to terminate. They have to stay on the Travelator all the way back to the quarter so the Elvi play an impromtu concert - 
The Blessed mother spoke to me today
Her smile kept my troubles at bay,
To her I wish to say
Abort and we’ll blow you away.
Blessed Mother meets Parliament 
They arrive in the quarter to pandamonium. The Elvi are coming to terms with the death of the great sage Kleo. They are screaming, crying, pulling their hair out. Kleo killed by the Jesus!
They want to see the sages andn find out they are in the Parliament building. (former brothel - The Vulva Las Vegas). Cracker makes a joke about a pack of cunts still working there and laughs loudly - but stops after he realises it is inappropriate and the Elvi are staring at him. 
The crowd treats them with reverence - Cracker takes the piss by saying things like “Make way, Blessed Mother coming through” He thinks the adoration is a bit of a joke, but says he does respect the Elvi as they are the only thing that make the PTD tolerable - he says imagine a world without An Elvis.
They are welcomed with open arms by the fledgling government. They are discussing fiscal policy and where they are going to invest. The treasurer reminds him to spread out their exposeure - the High Elvis says they have engaged the geniuses at “Spread Doctor.”
The Elvi are in awe when the Great Teacher and the Holy Mother are introduced to the Parliament. Sarah says she wishes to have a private word with Chilo and Silo. They don’t try to make excuses and Silo confesses to using a “Home cloing kit” (invented by Linus Grawling so it has some evil credibility - also these kits never work properly and it was only the virus that had made the perfect Dawkins clone. She tells them on the same night she was exposed to artifical DNA that had attached itself to the child’s DNA - there is no tell how the child will turn out. (The High Elvis later says he doesn’t care if the child has tenticles - they will have their saviour)
The High Elvis says the Elvi Parliament does not have the moral authority to punish Chilo and Silo.
They are invited to the funeral celebration for Kleoboulos and Cracker asks if he can bring along the Holy Aunties - Holy Aunt Hayley and Holy Aunt Kathy. The Elvis’s all want to be seen in the presense of the prophets.
Farwell Kleo
Kleo’s funeral takes place in the old crumbling sports stadium. They all sing “The Eight concentric circle of Dante’s Hell” (Heartbreak Hotel) It’s big.
Women’s Business
Sarah discusses with Hayley her abort/don’t abort problem. She tells her to consider random allocation.
Eloise
Sarah puts herself up for random allocation but the process has been co-opted and she is allocated to Alexander Shakti, L.5. She is horrified and spends most of the day in a foetal position. A knock on the door and when she opens it a big goon forces his way in, followed by a well dress woman in her 50’s. Sarah quickly gets the better of him and breaks his arm before chucking him out the door. She then turns the woman who introduces herself as Eloise Shakti. She smells a rat, Sarah is stunning, well credentialled and has money and great prospects - Why would you agree to marry my son? She tries to think up some plausable bullshit, but tells he she is pregnant. She thinks she will be rejected by the family, but Eloise says she has been waiting years to dump Shakti on someone and would not call off the allocation. She is happy Sarah is pregnant with someone else’s child because she could not bear a repeat of the genetic car crash that is Shakti. She tells Sarah to consummate the relationship immediately so Shakti will think the child is his.
Sarah makes arrangements to see Shakti. He was a virgin and she tricks him into thinking they have had sex. (Grandiose wank/reverse cowgirl) She was careful not to pass on the virus (No Super Shakti’s please)
Chapter 35 - Gravity Well Wedding
Gravity Well
The Johnny is brought into Sarah’s office and she presents him with the second disc and asks him to examine/test the two discs they now have in their possession. He isn’t keen, but agrees and is set up in a couple of labs and is given the instruction NOT to spin the discs otherwse it may produce a gravity well.
- - -
Later Sarah and Hayley meet with Agent Jones and they are told the PTD is digging up the old Hardy labs to obtain a virus to kill off the Elvi. He explains they are planning to target the Elvis genome and will have to kidnap a few Elvi to test the virus’ they develop. 
- - -
In a meeting with the Elvi, Hayley tells of the planned genocide of the Elvi. There is a race to see if they can get to the labs first (somehow) and destroy the samples. 
- - -
A later meeting they try to work out a way of getting to the undergrounds labs. They are examining maps of the city, blueprints of surrounding buildings. The maps are a little out of date and Cracker notes that one of the nearby buildings was the site of the bombing. The building had to be demolished and was now a giant square hole in the ground - very deep. It is so deep, that you could dig a largely horizonal tunnel directly under the labs. Apart from pipes and conduits, it is a straight line to the labs.
- - -
Cracker meets up with the owner of the demolished building. He had been denied insurance (terrorist attack) and Cracker gets permission to access the site with the promise of Elvi money.
- - -
At the Johnny’s lab they are clearing the smoke and dousing flames. Johnny decided to spin one of the discs and it resulted in blue lightening bursts exploding concrete and smashing through ballistic glass. There is a noticeable pattern left on one of the walls.
- - -
A scientist reports to Director Hardman on the progress of the virus development. They made a virus that only killed red-heads. He orders the virus be stored away - he is not keen on redheads and thinks they probably won’t be missed.
He then contacts Agent Jones for an update on the drilling/digging. To protect the PTD they had to erect an airtight structure on the drill site before drilling took place. They had got 5 metres down with laser cutters and plasma lances, but had resorted to percussion drills because he wanted to go slowly in order to ensure they don’t unleash Armageddon (and to give the Elvi a chance to get there first).
- - -
The Elvi construct a massive stage across the front of the site of the demolished building. Effectively obscuring any view into the giant hole. They are holding benefit concert and have drawn a massive crowd - mostly Dawks - because no-one has ever heard of a benefit concert. The concert covers the noise of the excavation below.
The Elvi donate the money to the owner of the building and contract to invest in the reconstruction of the building. With the backing of the Elvi he is now able to secure loans. 
