        <Document ID="F42C3F7C-F4AE-4B14-90DB-1F6B555AA84A">
            <Title>Pre-Emptive Reciprocity</Title>
            <Synopsis>Introducing the incompetence of Agent Jones and intro to the workings of the "Directorate of Pro-active euthenasia and Pre-emptive Reciprocity".  I like the Directorate name.
Also gives an idea of how important the discs are.  He is told to find the missing blank and the missing disc.  This could easily be incorporated elsewhere or perhaps dumped.  
</Synopsis>
            <Text>Pre-emptive Reciprocity
For the dark man the 216 floor trip to street level seemed to take forever. He was in the starting blocks and was sprinting even before the doors were fully open, a particle pulse pistol was now in his hand as he charged out to the street, but there was no-one there. Not the meat wagon and not the blank. Economy be damned! The blank was supposed to be waiting. He really wished that just one of these jobs wasn’t a cluster fuck, but they always were. Always. He wasn’t looking forward to filing this report, the Director was not going to be happy.
* * *
“Let me get this straight, Agent Jones.” said the incredulous Director of Pre-Emptive Reciprocity and Pro-active Euthanasia. (P.R.P.E.) “The blank lost the Gyges disc and you lost the blank. Does that about sum it up?”
“I wouldn’t chose to describe it in those terms” replied the soon to be demoted field operative. “The blank was really unwell. He could barely stand, but insisted on being juiced up with AMT to complete the contract. He made it look like suicide, but he somehow dropped the disc. I went up to retrieve it, but the office had been sanitized and a new tenant had moved in.”
“You idiot. You could be identified.”
“No, I had my disc. Security records would have been scrambled.”
“I mean by people in the building. Did you speak to anyone?” The director could not believe a fully trained agent could be this obtuse.
“No…..No I didn’t.” He figured he had better start lying. This truth telling bullshit was getting him nowhere. He decided to keep the cleaner out of it, at least until he knew what this street sweeper had pinched from Mr. Lee’s office.
“What happened with the blank?” The Director inquired.
“He had finished the job, there was a company meat-wagon around the corner and I was about to pop him off, when we discovered the cloak (disc) was missing. I went to fetch it and when I got back he was gone and so was the van.”
“So you lost the blank, a cloak and a van. A good days work and it’s not even midday.” The director stared him down. “This was a baby-sitting job, Agent Jones. He kills them, you kill him. Easy. You had better find that blank and silence him.”
“And the disc?”
“Find that too. We can’t have just anyone waltzing through secure zones at will. Violating the privacy of citizens is our job.”
“Yes, sir.” Agent Jones said, very glad this conversation was over.</Text>
        </Document>
