        <Document ID="47BFC090-DDE4-4CBE-9E11-A2566852C322">
            <Title> A Good Time to Patch up</Title>
            <Synopsis>DNA examination of the sample (yes the morgue is well resourced) shows that the child is a clone of a person named Richard Dawkins.
She also notes added DNA sequences (from the disc)
They conclude the Sages are behind it.
Dr Logan explains there are black market cloning devices.</Synopsis>
            <Text>A Good Time to Patch Up
8 to 10 days after bombing
“It took me ages to reconstruct the genetic lines but I can unequivocally say the sample dates back from the first half of the 20th century. You are carrying the clone of a long deceased man named Richard Dawkins, but there appears to be a few added sequences.” 
“The Dawkins!” Cracker hit the floor laughing and did not stop until his stomach muscles threatened to tear and his face ached. “The fuckin’ Dawkins!”
“I am looking at the helix and it is perfect, I mean absolutely zero copying errors – there are usually a one or two, but in this case the sequence is flawless. I will have to isolate and analyse the added sequences. That will take some considerable time.” Her eyes remained glued to the holograms as they hung in the air. The Hybrid T-Virus was already working on the growing embryo, correcting any errors and maximising development in-utero, seamlessly blending artificial DNA with the base genetic material of the clone. 
Dr Logan, on the other hand had just been hit with a wave of MDMA and was running between the two hugging them and sincerely saying, “I love you.” 
“Richard Dawkins? What did those creeps do to me?” Sarah was replaying the events on the travelator, but could not immediately pin down anything in particular. She did not know whether to laugh or cry, but did neither. She had not thought she would ever find herself in such a predicament and had no contingency plan whatsoever. “How can it be done without me noticing?”
“It does seem unlikely, but I suppose it is a possibility. There are black market cloning devices, but they don’t usually get such quality results. They keep the clone in stasis until implantation, without refrigeration. It implants the duplicate into the uterus directly through the abdominal wall. Anyone can manage it, once it is placed on the stomach, it automatically penetrates and implants. All in the matter of half a second.” Kathy took Sarah’s hand and held it lightly. “Sarah, you have been violated, far worse than any mere assault. You should contact the police.”
“Thank you, Kathy. I appreciate your kindness. I will seek my own justice on this one, thank you.” Sarah did not know how she could possibly face her new colleagues if this was to get out. She began planning a visit to old Kleo and the gang on the travelator very soon. 
“I don’t know what to say.” The gravity of the situation had suddenly hit Cracker. Now that he knew she was pregnant, an entirely new Sarah stood before him and he found his symmetry completely askew. In his immature youth he would have insisted the parasitic tumour-with-legs be treated with immediate removal. Only after the malignancy was excised could he look upon the woman as anything other than a diseased patient seeking a cure. Now, however, with Sarah standing before him, he saw a vulnerable, frightened girl in profound crisis. He wanted to take her in his arms, hold her close, assure her that everything will be alright and then sit her in a comfy chair with a nice cup of tea. He was muddled and kind of grossed out by these warm and fuzzy feelings. “What are you going to do?”
“I don’t know. I will have to think about it.” Sarah started walking toward to front security doors to disappear into the night. “Don’t follow me.” Her voice fading as she trudged away.
“That did not go well, did it Cracker?” Kathy cuddled up and he hugged her back. “You like her, huh?”
“She must not come to any harm.” 
“Always the protector.” She hugged him harder. “Want to go patching?”
“Yep.”</Text>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="960F6520-DC12-4012-A459-F106D6BB62E7">
            <Title>Hayley Lanning</Title>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="1F433A8F-6123-4B3F-BB21-8C67637FE379">
            <Title>Eloise Shakti CEO</Title>
            <Text>		It would seem that the conditions precedent for the end of the universe -Discovery of the disks once the disks are discovered/created annihilation is inevitable. All who have tried to stop the inevitability have failed. But they have the Dawkins and the Elvi Nation.
		Initial attempts to download the information, crashes the computer capacity of the lab and the information was lost. The information is dumped at once, sort of a zip file with the information enclosed in packets of data once opened.
		Have to use the quatum bio-processors of the Hardy control centre as they have the capacity to handle the data, but the memory of the computer has to be all but wiped or transferred to another site.
		For the system to handle the information, Richard has to act as a biological buffer for serialising and marshalling the vast information dump.
		Some sort of double dealing with Eloise to use her computers to dump the finance database to her computers. She will think she has got control, but when she tries to fire it up, she will discover that she cannot open the system without DNA key code. 
		When the transfer happens Richard will be wired to the system with from various contact points on his head.He tells them not to stop the transfer no matter what. Stopping mid stream could pop him out of existence or he could possibly jump time lines. The transfer is slow at first and then he begins to glow, low at first, but as he glows brighter the data transfer rate increases and he glows brighter and brighter. Gravity seems to increase and the become heavier and heavier. Furniture begins to buckle and squish diagonally down towards the bunker. They all begin to freak out and big debate as to whether to stop. Eventually Johnny tries and fighting against the gravity he almost hits the “stop” button - somehow thwarted.
		Richard finally glows less and less until you can see him - a grown man in his mid 20’s. Due to time dilation it was only 10minutes for the occupants of the bunker but 20 years for Richard. Q’s about how? “My brain had to grow (evolve) to cope with the data and the nature of the gravity well slowed down time for him and he had time to process the information. He 
		When the fridge guys arrive they are aghast. “Do you know what could have happened if you spin the dics? You could have collapsed the entire universe. How It did not happen is impossible!” “Maybe we are all dead” said Cracker. Richard, now a full grown adult confirms Cracker’s idea of inoculating one with the Panacea virus and one with the Panacea Anti-virus proves to be correct and the transfer is successful. 
		Johnny gets dealt with - no acknowledgement of any part of the discovery of multi-verses (or a series of big-bang/big crunch universes)
		The information is vast but all earths end the same way. The discovery of the discs always precede the eventual demise of the universe, just the amount of time it takes differs. The player are pretty much the same in the other multi-verses, but in the PTD there is an extra character - The Dawkins - they a are involved with the examination of the discs in the PTD. 

</Text>
