            <Title>Changing Brooms</Title>
            <Text>  
CHANGING BROOMS
14 hours before bombing - 9 months BTD
“The reformer has enemies in all who profit by the old order and only lukewarm defenders in all those who would profit by the new order” Machiavelli, The Prince, 1513.
_ _ _
Recruitment Policy was not something that often occupied the mind of Tony “Cracker” Hardy, Cleaner, Level 2, or any of his low-born peers. Blue collar scum like him possessed little knowledge or interest in things HR and were too ignorant to appreciate the significance of Corporate Strategic Direction, Organisational Goals, Selection Criteria, Key Result Areas or any of the other fallacious constructs created to justify bloated recruiting departments. ??????????? 
Jagging some unexpected work in the management district had obvious advantages, especially in an office above the layer – there was an actual view out of the window. You could see clear across to the next building and several hundred metres beyond! Swarms of Hover-copts flitted about between monolithic glass-clad structures, rising sharply and dropping suddenly to rest gently, but fleetingly, on the pin-pong bat landing pads jutting out willy-nilly into the cluttered airspace. 
As a child he had seen a hover-copt up close when two burning wrecks fell from of the sky and crashed into the neighbouring apartment block, before falling to the street. He and his fellow hooligans examined the wreckage with childish exuberance, amused the intensity of the blaze had burned the lips clean off of the deceased occupants, giving each a gleaming Colgate grin. They laughed and pointed at the dead rich people, all smiling at their fate. Cracker and his mates were delighted to see the adults present were also amused by the carnage. Just as these thoughts began to fade away he saw two hover-copts collide at great speed, the tangled mess burning and breaking up as it passed into the layer and out of sight. A fiery ring spread out across “the layer”, creating a massive fissure 100 metres across, before petering out as the hole slowly closed shut. 
* * *
‘The layer’ was a permanent thick cloud of condensation, emissions and miscellaneous airborne particulate matter that barely allowed rays of sunlight to penetrate and strike the ground 216 floors below. Decade upon decade of fossil fuel emissions, chemical misuse, pesticides and cow farts had pushed the atmosphere well beyond the point of no return. No meaningful attempt was made to reverse the degradation of the environment. There was no profit in that. The natural and according to the company, rational course of action, was to spew yet more noxious chemicals into the atmosphere. Unprecedented amounts of “air-cleaner” over extended periods. The sales pitch to the world was “total atmospheric clarification”. Clean air, clean living and, with “Marlborough Country” ads once again possible, a surge in cigarette sales. 
Sales went beyond anyone’s wildest expectations. Financially, the company and the Primary Trade Dominion really cleaned up, unfortunately however, the atmosphere did not. Rather than clarifying” the air, all pollutants condensed together at about 200 metres above sea level. The floating pea-soup acid-mist represented the sum of all the filth and foul muck ever spewed out of a smoke stack, exhaust pipe, chimney or cow’s bum. Pure concentrated evil. 
Governments from all over the world protested, sent envoys and some even threatened military action. The CEO of the PTD laughed at that prospect. No one would attack from the west, it was a nuclear wasteland and PTD now manufactured most of the world’s armaments and all of the high-tech bio-weapons. Very few had the balls to attack and even fewer had sufficient armaments to sustain such unwise undertaking. The company explained to their disgruntled customers that the process had not failed, it had merely worked in an unexpected way. The final desired result would merely take a little longer and require the purchase of more product. With the addition of a little dye in the mixture, “the layer” was changed from spew green to a pleasant silvery white hue. Apart from the aesthetic improvement, the extra purchases did nothing. 
* * *
Management never descended to street level to walk among working class slime, instead using hover-copts to jump between buildings many, many times per day in order to attend meetings or just to be seen at the right restaurant with the right people. Mid-air collisions were a regular occurrence and considered a fact of life, the price of avoiding the common man. The elite would rather die in a flaming wreck, than, by choice, breath the same oxygen-starved air as their working class underlings.
“Did you see that?” Cracker yelled out without thinking as he watched the layer close shut and the mangled copters disappear. It was not forbidden, just plain unwise for a working class stiff to initiate conversation with the superior members of the management elite. A few eyebrows raised as they, too, saw the copters drop out of the sky, but without comment most went back to work, unphased by deaths just outside. The eyes that did not return to work remained fixed on the talkative cleaner, their heads shaking in disapproval at his inappropriate utterance. Cracker took this as an invitation to piss off somewhere else, which he did, shuffling to the big job in the office next door. 
He hoped they would not report him for his breach of work-place etiquette, he really needed the job. The principal benefit gained by Cracker during his present cleaning engagement was gazing upon the many stunning examples of female kind that filled the entire building. It seemed clear, at least to Cracker, that the company selected employees on looks alone and from his present perspective, the policy could not criticised. The Finance Department seemed to favour large breasts, whereas tall blondes filled almost every seat in the Cyber-Security Division. As he moved from one Department to the next he noted with increasing delight, that almost every seat was occupied by a female backside. Men, at least in this little corner of corporate life, were not wanted. For reasons that no one ever bothered to work out, women worked for an average of 26% less than their greedy male counterparts and an HR manager were mad not to take advantage. 
Cracker was just finishing off his final job for the morning, another executive having opted for the suicide retirement package, when Sarah Jacobson strolled off the elevator. She was stunning in every way and left a trail of slack-jawed gawkers, both male and female, in her wake. It was her first day in new position as Cyber Security Manager Level 5 and was making an immediate impression. Her eyes were a piercing pale blue that penetrated to your core, causing heart palpitations and many women to seriously re-assess their sexual orientation. Her hair, one of the concessions she made to the artificial beauty, was a cascade of pure white sand, wildly glistening with random prisms of light and colour as she strode under the glare of the down-lights. Although the concept of a deity had been officially rejected decades prior, her legs, hips and breasts were proof positive of the existence of God. It was her face, however, that quite literally knocked Cracker backwards. Her natural beauty required no cosmetic enhancement – high cheek bones, unblemished glowing skin, faultless white teeth that formed the perfect smile. And the perfume, pure, permeating and yet not overpowering. He could not help but fall in lust immediately.
He already knew what he was going to tell his drinking buddies – You should have seen this girl. You’d crawl across 3 k’s of broken glass just to suck the cock that fucked her! He knew it wasn’t exactly original and could not remember where he had first heard it, but she was literally that beautiful. Now all he had to do was locate 3 kilometres of broken glass and a bottle of mouthwash.
Looking at the complete package (it was impossible not to) and exhaling with a melancholy sigh, Cracker knew that he would never get his level two hands anywhere near her. A short conversation was his highest expectation. After all, she would have to be Level 4 or 5 to work here and self-employed grunts could only hope to get to level 3 at most. He caught sight of his reflection in the mirror hidden behind the door. His white overalls bore the name “Cracker Jack Cleaning Service” thereby branding him as a commoner, a mere worker – a pleb. The large split in the posterior, a legacy of poor tailoring and an expanding backside, gave all and sundry an unflattering and most unwelcome view of his boxers. Branding him, not only a grunt, but a most objectionable one - even if he was wearing his good underwear. He knew the overalls were too small when he had put them on, but they were the only ones available when the call came in. It had not been expected that the job would take so long, but John Lee (the name was still on the door), had really done a number on himself. He was not content to kill himself with a handgun, no - he had to use a truly messy and antiquated shotgun. His brains were, literally, on every surface and sanitising the room before her arrival had proved impossible. 
 Cracker could not believe the mess. Who used firearms these days? Too messy, too loud and entirely inaccurate. Particle-pulse weapons were far cleaner, quieter and deadly accurate. While the weapon was just as lethal as the antiquated expanding gas-projectile models, pulse particle beams had the supplementary characteristic of fusing and sealing wounds. No bothersome rivers of blood to clean up. Just drag the body out, give the floor a quick mop and you’re ready for business. Cracker loved those jobs – easy money. Having now seen her, he was glad the idiot had splattered himself.
As Sarah walked towards the office, Cracker’s mind started racing, frantically searching his brain for something witty and original to say - something that would set him apart from the crowd – something whimsical, yet pithy.
She entered. “How long will you be? I was told the office would be ready by now.” 
He was desperately trying to hide his arse by backing up to the wall. Now was his chance, “Shotgun.” was all he managed to get out.
“What?” 
He tried again, but nothing came out. Sarah knew the effect she had on men, but she was not going to make this easy for him. You can fuck with their minds “real easy” her sister used to tell her. “Men ain’t nothin’ but dicks and hormones. No brains…” She lost her train of thought, being distracted by the enigmatic behaviour of the cleaner. Exactly why was he rubbing his backside against the wall? No Brains? You may be right sis, you may be right. 
“Have you spoken in English before L.1?” She smiled in mild amusement.
Still trying to hide his tail, he made a failed attempt at composure. “Yes, English. Mr. Lee used a shotgun ma’am and, without going into the gory details, it takes a while to get all the bits and pieces.” An entire sentence, he was quite pleased.
Surprised by the glimmer intelligence she continued with the pointless chatter, “Shot gun? I don’t want to find anything nasty on the wall do I? Or worse still, get a stain on my outfit.” She smiled brightly and Cracker heart thumped loudly.
“I know all about that, brains are a bastard to get out.” He was feeling slightly less stupid now, although he silently acknowledged that enlightening her on the finer points of brain-stain removal probably wasn’t the best topic to pursue. Sarah saw his discomfort, and upon sighting his rather fashionable boxer shorts, she was amused and even a little flattered by his embarrassment. 
“When I have someone’s frontal lobes splattered all over me I’ll know who to call.” She was enjoying this game now. “You should use that in advertisements” 
“Yes, I can see it now, ‘Cracker’s Cleaning Service – Splattered Brains, but no Stains’ ” He quipped, surprised at the speed of his reply. “I have your permission to use it then, ma’am?”
“Please don’t call me that. I’m Sarah Jacobson, PhD, L.5. When will the office be ready, L.1?” 
He said, “This L.2 will be just a few minutes.” 
“L.2? I would not have guessed.” She looked at the split in his trousers and was greatly amused. “Well, L.2, I’ll just start working and you can finish up. I won’t need any of his personal trinkets, could you pick up it all up and throw it all out with the waste paper?” She suggested. Although it wasn’t really paper, more like a thin polymer sheet that could accept ink. She knew he would have to cross the room to collect the refuse, maximising the exposure of his undergarments and his embarrassment. She loved messing with men’s heads, they were all such dullards and offered up no end of amusement.
“No….um I mean, yes. I’ll have to give the room a once over, alone, before I can give you the all clear.” He replied. “Regulations ma’am… ah Sarah.” Nice recovery, moron. 
By now Sarah was at her desk and all attempts by Cracker at hiding his shame were useless and becoming increasingly ridiculous. However, he continued the farce by drawing the steam cleaner behind him, casually trying to shroud himself in a cloud of steam. The steam emerged from between his legs as the hottest and wettest fart ever released from captivity. 
“What is your name L.2?” She said, deciding to ignore the shot-of-steam comedy hour. She placed her briefcase on her desk, and placed her hand on a black polymer sensor at the side of her desk and within a few microseconds her DNA had been confirmed and the holo-screen burst into life. 
“Sticking with holo-screens are you?” Cracker observed. “Where’s your beta-max?” 
Sarah decided to ignore the critic. The introduction of holo-screen was greeted with much enthusiasm by the meme-centric upper class, breaking all sales records, but they turned out to be a bit of a wank. They were really only useful if you had to examine objects in 3D day. Medicine, architecture, academia and of course the porn industry had a legitimate need for this technology, but few others. Most financial and business records were steadfastly stuck in 2D territory and consequently holo-screens were an unnecessary expense for the average business. In any case, no boss wanted his workers constantly distracted by porn stars, floating above each desk, the money shots where just too life-like. Sales of these devices stalled and then fell off all together. Although most went back to using the glass screen, a standard for decades, porn addicts still had one tucked away at home, for those critical times when the wife was out. 
The familiar monotone of the web-voice came alive and immediately displayed a number of messages for Sarah on the holographic display. Mostly they related to her old position, but one notified her that her promotional med-exam was at 4.00pm that day. Promotions were never confirmed without a clean bill of health. 
The computer then defaulted to recounting latest lists of available properties to lease or buy. A quick glance at this list of available properties revealed that Mr. Lee’s apartment was already up for lease. He’s only been dead 7 hours! It’s in a good building and above cloud level too. I’ll have to look into it, in fact I’ll take it. She made an on-line bid and the property was hers. She did not consider whether Mr. Lee had a family or what their fate might be. It was not that she was totally devoid of human sympathy, it was that these type things were not considered important by the company and, consequentially, by anyone else. If the company did not worry about these things, the individual should not concern themselves either. If his death brought more profit, then the death was worthwhile, even necessary. Everyone knew that.
“My name’s Tony Hardy, but everyone calls me Cracker.” 
“I’m sorry?” She was still thinking about her new apartment.
“Tony Hardy, but everyone calls me Cracker.”
 
“Cracker….oh I see, yes. Crack-a-hardy! Very level 1.” She knew this comment would wound him, but she was surprised at the level of pity she felt for this commoner. “Keep the common in place – keep the company in black,” she reminded herself. 
For a short time Cracker had thought she might actually be a nice person, but she had not let the opportunity go by without rubbing it in. Fucken level 5’s, he thought. The new rich were no better than anyone else was, but they acted as if their bowels made birthday cake. I would like to get through just one day without being reminded. An accident of birth and I’m fucked for life. (An accident that could only be rectified under extremely rare circumstances and never without help.)  It was rare for a common man to run a flourishing business. Usually, they were absorbed in hostile takeovers or crushed under-foot before they had the opportunity. This had two desired effects. Firstly, it reduced the likelihood of any meaningful competition and, secondly, it reduced the number of candidates for confirmation to upper levels. 
“I said I’m not level 1.” Cracker retorted indignantly. “If my business keeps going I could be looking at level 3 within a year.” As if she would believe it – he wasn’t even sure that he believed it. The fact that he could not afford to have his clothes repaired did not assist the veracity of his claim. 
“I’m sorry, I didn’t mean to be rude. As you can tell…” Looking at the name ‘Lee’ on the door, “I’m new here and I’m a bit nervous. Mr. Lee’s decision to retire early got me to level 5. I received the call at 6.00am this morning. One minute I was Cyber-Security level 4 and the next I’m level 5 manager. Who would have guessed?” Why am I giving him my resume? He is just a commoner and there is no point in continuing this. He does have a cute bum, though. 
“Yeah, I’ve been up all night too. I got the call at 4.00am. I was told to get the office ready for the new computer virtuoso. Been marked for bigger and better things, eh?” Cracker confided. Whoops, too much information. I hope she doesn’t ask.
“Who told you that?” She blurted out, concerned about her privacy more than where the information came from. Who would think it was appropriate to discuss her C.V. with a cleaner? Conveniently ignoring she had just done precisely the same thing.
“Ma’am. I’m not at liberty to discuss that.” He said sheepishly. She did not reply, but leaned forward just enough for him to get a brief, but tasteful glimpse of her bra. I knew lingerie would come in handy.
Cracker stood there motionless for what seemed like an eternity. He knew she had put on the show for him and he was in big trouble. His desperate attempts not to look amused her greatly. They are just dicks and hormones. Admirably he averted his gaze for an inordinate length of time. Fully 10 seconds elapsed before his eyes betrayed him. Immediately upon catching a glimpse, he felt the familiar twinge in his crotch, the rush of blood and the unwanted expansion. If he was going to walk away with any dignity he had to disencumber himself from the conversation immediately. An L.2. Sporting a stiffy, in a building full of Level 5’s, was asking to be thrown out a window.
She leaned back, taking away the view, and said, “I would like to know how a cleaner would know anything about me?” She leaned forward again. His organ continued to expand and was threatening to bust through his boxers.
“Okay, okay. I got the call from Shakti. He’s in Homicide. Whenever there is a late night job, he calls me in and I get the cleaning job. That’s it. He had heard that the new girl was a real high-flyer.”
Unable to think why the name was familiar to her she merely replied, “I gather he gets a kickback from you.” 
“No.” He said, hoping he got away with the lie. “I don’t mess with any of the evidence. I’m never late. I get the job done quickly, so that you can get on with the job of making money.” He continued to lie. She was immediately reminded of a slogan from her school days: Everything is money and money is everything. 
Lieutenant Shakti was the public face of the Department of Traffic Movement and Public Security, formerly known as the Police. He appeared in all of the recruiting advertisements, made public affairs announcements and was now making a name for himself as a homicide investigator. The fact that he had been called to a run-of-the-mill suicide seemed odd, but if it was something more sinister, the entire floor would still be crawling with cops, robots, flashing lights and all manner of devices that beeped. 
“Well, I’ll get someone to make me a Café-Chai-Tea-cino and let you finish up.” As Sarah left the office Cracker’s eyes inadvertently followed. It was the first time he had been directly behind her and he decided that, yes, she was the most beautiful woman he had ever seen – a manifestation of human perfection. With her gone, he was able to concentrate on deflating his penis and finishing up. He gave her desk the once over, gathered up the notes, scrawls and bric-a-brac Lee had left on his desk and fled as soon as he could, hoping not to run into her on the way out. 
As he pushed the trolley towards the obscure rear elevators, the “tradesman’s” exit, he heard Sarah’s voice from behind. “Nice underwear, Mr Hardy.”
“I could say the same to you.” He was happy with his reply.
“I am shocked Mr Hardy.” She decided that, social levels notwithstanding, she liked this fellow. She liked to laugh and he was hilarious, even if most of his humour was inadvertent. I think I’ll call him the accidental comedian. 
She checked that the door was locked; (they had already transferred her security codes) and made sure it was set to opaque, before she allowed herself to relax and raise her arms triumphantly above her head. She was on her way up. It was of no concern that her career had gathered momentum due to Mr. Lee’s bout of depression. Now she had to work out what she was supposed to do. She had only been told to report to her new office at 8.00am, nothing more. She looked up at the door and made a mental note to change the name as soon as possible. For some reason she was reminded of all the ancient black and white spy vids she had endlessly devoured as a child. “Cloak and dagger” they had called it, hadn’t they?</Text>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="19103B49-573F-4E69-B664-57F95E1FD2A4">
            <Title>Shakti does something right</Title>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="A29CED6D-74DD-4843-96F9-49BB7DE3A2B1">
            <Title>The Johnny</Title>
            <Synopsis>I don't like the name "The Johnny" either.  Should be changed, but his surname should be kept.
The part is for Sarah to infect the bio-matter in the disc.
Infect Cracker with the virus.
Get more information on the disc.
Get an idea of where Cracker lives.  
I mention Sarah was impressed by Cracker's ability to make a bed.  This is supposed to allude to her "nesting" as she is pregnant.  I don't think that worked</Synopsis>
            <Text>The Johnny
Night After the Bombing
Unloading “The Johnny”, as Cracker had decided to call him, was nowhere near as difficult as predicted and they managed to lug him to Cracker’s apartment before he became fully aware. Cracker wanted to dump The Johnny, shit be his name, on what masqueraded as a couch. Sarah insisted he required a proper bed, but had to settle for Cracker’s lumpy array of metal springs and exposed stuffing that waited in the bedroom.
“Metal springs? Haven’t you heard of hydro-gel?” The Johnny was now awake.
“I suppose you want clean sheets as well?” Cracker thought sarcasm was widely known, but The Johnny lumbered out of the bed and onto the floor.
“Dirty sheets? Where am I?” The Johnny looked around and was filled with disgust. “This place is deplorable.”
“The decorator is coming next week.” Cracker was not warming to The Johnny at all.
“Have you got any?” Sarah inquired, but was met with a blank stare. “Clean Sheets?”
“Yes, yes.” Cracker stomped out of the room and returned with a set of sheets, still in its original plastic wrapping. He’d pinched them a few months back and had them ear-marked for Christmas presents. “Clean enough?”
Sarah and Cracker set to changing the sheets and to her immense surprise he seemed to know what he was doing, even though the task was made more difficult by the absence of a fitted sheet, he efficiently and skilfully scooted around the bed, each corner hospital standard. She stood back grinning and, as she watched, she became impressed, more than impressed, she felt herself admiring his domestic flair. It was very peculiar, she thought, to admire someone for their ability to make a bed. I’ve heard admiration is usually gained for one’s ability to mess up a bed. Oh, naughty thought. She giggled out loud before slapping a hand up to her lips.
They gave The Johnny the aggregate of pain-killers Cracker had lying around and, when ferreted out of sock drawers, plastic tubs hidden in his rickety kitchen cupboard and from under the sink, he had quite a little pharmacy. The Johnny was quickly zonked out on the cocktail of pills and his complaints settled to a soft murmur before he finally slept quietly.
Reflecting on their second outing, Cracker plonked himself in his couch and said, “A very strange day. I’ve forgotten why we went out in the first place.”
“The disc!” Sarah exclaimed, grabbing her breasts as she ran to the bathroom. “I completely forgot!” A lapse of memory was completely unknown to Sarah and the feeling was very deflating. Locking the door behind her she thrust her hand inside her bra. Nothing. She opened her shirt and pulled her bra aside and was shocked to see what appeared to be a superfluous nipple on her right breast. She leaned closer to the aged mirror, found a spot that was clear of gunk and was horrified to see that her skin had begun growing over the disc and the bio-components were taking root. “Cracker, wake Johnny up. I have a bit of a problem here.”
“He’s fast asleep, I can’t get a thing out of him.” Cracker said through the door a couple of minutes later. “What’s up?” 
The door unlocked and creaked open. Sarah motioned him in and was pale, sickly and frightened. “The disc is under my skin and I can feel it spreading out.”
“That cannot be good. Give me a look.” Cracker said innocently.
“I have no choice, but can you promise you will act like an adult?”
“Me? Absolutely.” 
Sarah opened her shirt and exposed her right breast. “It’s under the skin!”
Cracker looked closely upon the breast and even with an extra nipple it was truly magnificent to behold. He desperately wanted to grab that tit and give it a good squeeze. I really knead to. Ha, Ha. “I guess a doctor is out of the question?” 
“The disc would be too hard to explain.” She shook her head in resignation.
“Well whatever we do, we should do it fast.” Cracker hoped she had a plan, because in the presence of a bare breast, his brain refused to work.
“If we cut the skin, one side of the disc to the other, around the edge, we might be able to pull it out with tweezers.” Sarah said, detesting the idea.
“I have razor blades somewhere here”, he pointed around the room, but could not break eye-contact with nipple. 
“Would you mind getting it?” Grabbing either side of his face forcing him to look in her eyes. 
He took to the vanity cabinet like an alcoholic looking for that last hidden bottle, tearing out the contents of the cupboard and dumping drawers onto the floor before he located a packet of ancient double edged wafer thin blades. He quickly handed them to Sarah and returned to the important business of staring at an exposed breast. 
“I will hold it still and you make a half-moon cut, right around the edge and I will see if I can squeeze it free.” Sarah grabbed her breast on either side of the disc and squeezed lightly. The disc popped up, pressed tight against the underside of the freshly grown skin. “Cut lightly, but with confidence.”
He was shaking but managed to make a single clean curved cut one third around the circumference. Sarah squeezed and massaged the flesh, as if popping a giant zit, but the disc wouldn’t budge. Cracker, maddened by the proximity of a bare breast, could take it no longer, without warning and purely on cave-man instinct, he began sucking on that tit like an alcoholic after he had found that last hidden bottle. It was unclear whether it was the vacuum of his mouth or Sarah’s disgust that dislodged the disc, but it began moving.
“Keep going, its coming. Got it, thank goodness.” Sarah was breathing heavily and was most relieved. 
“What’s going on Sarah?” The Johnny was at the door and Cracker was stuck fast, incrementally removing the disc with his mouth.
“This is definitely not what it seems.” Sarah was mortified, but remained still until the disc-ectomy was complete. 
Cracker turned around with the disc between his teeth, minuscule unseen drops of Sarah’s blood clinging to the shiny metal and his lips. His spat the offending alloy into the tiny grubby sink and carefully washed it clean, noting the disc seemed to be largely undamaged, but there were tiny tendrils half the width of a hair waving about like thirsty little leeches searching for a blood vessel. Incrementally they grew shorter before withdrawing completely into the metal, leaving a flawless gleaming surface. 
It took some pretty tricky explaining to satisfy The Johnny what he saw in the bathroom was a medical emergency, but Sarah managed to talk him around. 
“Yeah, I sucked it.” Cracker raised his right hand for a high five, but there were no takers. “C’mon, you guys, don’t leave me hanging.” He laughed boisterously, but was rightly ignored. 
Slightly groggy, the Johnny shook his head in disgust and returned to examining the disc with a magnifying glass and appeared intrigued by his observations. “How very interesting. Some of the bio-components seem to be missing, but if I am not mistaken, they are regenerating, Sarah.”
“I guess the missing bits are still swimming around inside me. What does that mean?” Sarah was troubled greatly and not feeling all that well, either. She had never been sick in her entire life and did not like the sensation of her body betraying her. Is this what it is like for normal people?
“I cannot even hazard a guess. The existence of these discs was only a rumour and as far as I know, self-repairing circuitry is science fiction. A bio-quantum processor is decades ahead of our current technology, so no-one will know what will happen to you Sarah. We are in unknown territory.” The Johnny was matter-of-fact about Sarah’s prospects. His head hurt too much to offer sympathy to another. “You will have to see a very discreet doctor and hope he doesn’t find anything wrong.” 
“No. Doctors have to report abnormal results. I will have to wait and hope for the best.” Sarah trusted her immune system would take care of any problems, but crossed her fingers for good measure. 
“It’s just a bit of goop. She’ll be right.” Cracker’s ignorance was vast and covered most topics.
“No, the goop, as you call it, is a biological emollient that is saturated with synthetic DNA. The program is embedded in the DNA and that DNA is in Sarah’s blood stream. There is no telling what will happen.”
“We will all have to stay here for the night and see what it does to me. I am too tired and sore to make the trip to the management district and we must discuss all of this further.” She was resigned to a night in the slums.
“There is no way I am staying in this cesspool, I’m going home. I need a bath and a glass of Merlot.” The Johnny didn’t find the idea any more palatable than Sarah.
“No, you have concussion. You must stay here as well. Cracker make sure he stays here.”
“The Johnny stays.”
“Cracker you may use violence” Sarah smiled.
“I am going to, even if he behaves.” Cracker’s reply made Sarah smile even wider.
“Good night, Johnny” Sarah pushed The Johnny in the direction of the one bedroom and crashed on the couch. Cracker took the bathroom and slept in the bath, a fate to which he had some considerable experience. He had long since taken to the practice of sleeping in the bath whenever he was enduring a bout of gastro-intestinal trouble. It was closer to the bowl and if he couldn’t safely traverse that small distance, he would just shit the bed. To some, a bathroom with a space wasting tub was an extravagance, but to Cracker it was a second bedroom with en-suite.</Text>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="C7B418AE-86BA-4259-B3D6-F6693FEE7B82">
            <Title>The Blank</Title>
        </Document>
