        <Document ID="86CA3C75-2E30-470F-93C2-617C90ACE2C2">
            <Title>The Dawkins</Title>
            <Synopsis>Second part of the Travelator series.
The Sages mention "The timing is perfect- 283 days exactly."  283 is the expected length of a pregnancy and they are also 283 days away from Christmas. They want their saviour born on Christmas day.  I think I have mentioned (later) that Richard is born on Christmas day.
Lots of Praising the Dawkins.  
The narrative of Kleo and the philosophy surrounding the Dawkins should remain, but it needs a little more pep.  Editing needed. 
Touches on the concept of certainty and the truth.  "When we embrace faith, the truth is locked down tight."
Touches on how truth is subverted - "Falsehood possesses an unending assortment of strategies.  The truth merely exists."
Touches upon how god may have been invented.
"The god being deliberately made us flawed and then set about punishing us for it."
Kleo makes the observation that economics is the religion of the PTD.
Explains how (actual) religion was removed from the PTD.  You may be amused or bemused by this explanation. Slightly ambiguous, too.
Bit worried about the attack on the travelator car.  It's a distraction to impregnate Sarah with the clone. I don't think it works - I am sure you can come up with a better idea.  (You later find out that Linus Grawling manufactured a device that injects the clone and implants it.  Luckily she has the virus, so any cloning errors are corrected in utero.)At this stage she still has the disc inside her bra.</Synopsis>
            <Text>
The Dawkins
Afternoon/evening after bombing
</Text>
        </Document>
