        <Document ID="9E3B968B-0E3E-43AE-809C-527EA1124C16">
            <Title>A Big Bang for the Big Bang</Title>
            <Synopsis>This is back in the bar at the time of the explosion.  Crackers mate, Halo, has picked up a girl and left with her.  Just outside of the building, the nightclub explodes.  She is a company agent AVI (someone) who had just planted the bomb.  She allowed herself to get picked up as she plans to fuck and kill him.  He had picked her up with the intention of fucking and killing her (not necessarily in that order).  I have them both planning to kill the other as they are fucking.
Halo has a special dagger, "The slice of life"  that is thin and hollow, so the blood really spurts out.  Direct rip-pff of "Steely Dan" the stainless steel dildo. (Although Steely Dan is a better idea.) This could easily be left out.  
The sex scene is okay, some of it can be re-written but I am generally okay with it.  
He goes back into the crush and finds Cracker's old girlfriend.  He later kills her.  As stated Cracker is arrested for her death some time later. 
As a whole, this chapter does not offend me too much.  I like the bit about Halo "He thought of himself a simple man with simple needs -  if he had a girl to fuck and stab, he was sweet."

The reason for the bombing is pretty lame.  (The CEO thinks Cracker is related to Jamison Hardy and may be a beneficiary to a fortune that he does not deserve.)</Synopsis>
            <Text>
Big Bang for the Big Bang
At time of bombing - year zero.
Halo had seen her on the far side of the bar, only minutes before the explosion. Under his expert gaze she looked wholly out of place; not that her outfit or hair was any more or less outrageous than the rest, it was an almost imperceptible purpose of action, laced with a signature detachment that had distinguished her. His keen eye told him she did not enter the club with dancing the night away on her mind. She was there for altogether another reason. He was by her side in a flash, unleashing a bizarre yet unavoidable stare, apparently overwhelming her defences. Unblinking, she dropped her bag and backed away slowly, turned and headed briskly for the exit with Halo in hot pursuit, grinning triumphantly, testosterone flooding his body. All thoughts of Sarah now purged from his mind, at least for the while. He knew Cracker did not have a chance with her, she was just slumming it with the peasants until something else took her fancy. 
Catching her at the foot of the massive stone columns at the eastern façade, she turned and with nothing said they kissed passionately, longingly and hungrily; both seemingly unable to get enough of each other’s face in their mouths. So lost in this rapture, they continued, even when the explosion knocked them over.
“Wow that was some kiss.” Halo was delirious, his mind spinning. She was as good as dead now. 
“To die for.” The Termocorp Agent said, panting, her chest bursting out of her dress with each breath drawn. Who is this fucker? He must have seen something. He must know something. Either way he’s as good as dead.
Her quarters were, of course, very small but nearby and clean. Not that comfort was foremost on their minds; they would have fucked on an anthill such was their mutual need. She was very compliant and had not baulked when the head of his cock gruffly commenced negotiations with her anus. Rather than surprise or anger, his back door assault was met with enthusiasm as she arched her back perfectly aiding penetration and before long, he was imposing himself with malevolent authority, their bodies slapping together loudly, balls and tits swinging riotously.
He increased the pace, thumping her head into the wall, her hand, under the pillow remained firmly rapped around her particle pistol. “Pound me!” You will be dead shortly, so enjoy it while you can.
His hand snaked to his jacket folded neatly at the end of the mattress and drew out a small glistening three sided stainless steel metal spike, he named Slice of Life. He caught a glimpse of his reflection in the mirror sheen of the blade and felt the rush. A weapon of his own design it tapered to sharp points at both ends, with a thicker rounded handle in the middle, it was hollow through the centre from end to end. It left a gaping wound that really allowed the blood to gush and Halo liked it, he like it a lot. In the mirror edge of the spike he caught a glimpse of a handgun. What the fuck? 
She turned her head to fire just as the spike plunged into her back, smashing her spine, separating ribs and annihilating her heart. Death took her quickly, not even granting her the dignity of getting off one shot. The blood did not jet out like usual. Apart from a few final pathetic flutters, the heart had already stopped pumping and there was no spurting blood or gurgling and gasping for that last breath. This was completely unsatisfactory. A hit to the lungs would, at the very least, have caused bright pink foam to ooze out of the wound and corner her mouth. Stabbing them in the neck was entirely more graphic, but the sight of the gun caused him to hurry and he was off target. His need had not been satiated. He finished off the fuck, but it didn’t make him feel any better. In fact, it made him angry. He was unable to come to terms with the fact some people simply did not know how to die properly.
Anger continued to surge and build until he took a closer look at the gun. It was company issue and only covert agents had particle pistols on personal issue. At that moment the realisation struck. He went white and his cock shriveled to a peanut; this was not just some random low, she was a company agent and she would be missed. He figured he had a few hours before anyone would be looking for her and he used that time to clean the entire apartment. It did not take too long as she was a very good housekeeper. Satisfied that he had left no physical evidence behind he withdrew quietly and set off into the night. He had unfinished business and was keen to find some more clients. 
An enormous crowd had gathered on the street. A target rich environment for a serial killer out on the town. He decided to wade in and stab a few, just to watch some blood flow, but it still was insufficient to sate his need. He could covertly slice someone at random, but he had to melt back into the crowd far too quickly, allowing him no time to savour the moment - to see the surprise and horror in their faces. He was resigned to beating off to snuff vids at home when he spied a familiar face in the crowd. It was that Cracker’s ex, Angela. She had been on his list for a while and he long wanted that cunt to feel his wrath. He managed to skirt around her without being noticed and then did an about face and headed in her direction. She was deep in thought when they bumped into each other. He immediately noticed the fear in her eyes and knew he had a good chance of whisking her away.
“Halo? Do you know what is going on? Where did all these people come from?” Angela was clearly distressed. “My fiancé just disappeared a few minutes ago. He was right next to me and then he was gone.”
The thought struck Halo that he had probably just stabbed her betrothed. What a bonus! He tried desperately to squash the evil grin that was etching across his face. 
 “He must have lost his footing and….and got trampled!” She grabbed Halo and sobbed uncontrollably, her tears and snot fucking up a perfectly good jacket. He was, of course, disgusted by this childish display, but he was keen fuck her and kill her (or kill her and fuck her – either way was good) so he drew her close and held her gently.
She looked into his eyes, “I think we might be in serious trouble. We could be crushed if we don’t get out of this crowd.” Almost automatically Halo’s upgraded eyes went to work, incrementally changing colour and pattern with every blink, until finding to right pattern – the key that unlocked the sum of all her neuroses and quickly morphed her into soft pliable putty.
Halo, still holding her close, immediately considered a couple of things. Firstly he was amazed that he not cracked a fat (even if she was a cunt she was still very attractive) and secondly he had stupidly squeezed into this crowd without so much as a single thought about the danger. He looked around and suddenly he knew that the situation was serious and yes, they were in genuine and imminent peril. His mind raced – there was no way out unless you were close to your apartment block or, he thought with glee, if you were close to an apartment block where you had just killed someone and had the access codes! 
“Come with me, sweet-heart. I will take good care of you. I have friend nearby.” He said in soothing, calm tones and took her by the hand, heading back to the scene of the crime or, rather, soon to be scene of the crimes. He was overwhelmed with anticipation, his mind filled with deplorable images of shocking violence. In short, he was happy. He thought himself a simple man with simple needs – if he had a girl to fuck and stab, he was sweet.

</Text>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="5B088B8A-1C5F-488D-B35E-928299617769">
            <Title>Paternal Mystery</Title>
            <Synopsis>This is all about Sarah finding out she is pregnant.
She initially thinks Cracker must have raped her somehow.
They get a sample of the foetus and find out that Cracker is not the father and Sarah is not the mother.</Synopsis>
            <Text>Paternal Mystery
8 to 10 days after bombing
Cracker did not see the combination of punches that rained upon him in the seconds after Sarah heard the happy news. He was knocked out after the first fist struck his chin, the rest were just for good measure. 
“You rapist!” Sarah yelled through a torrent of tears as Cracker came back to consciousness. “I’m pregnant! To you? You disgust me.” How he managed to do it without waking her she did not know. She could not remember any chance he had to drug her. Maybe a patch? “My DNA mixed with yours?” She began to gag. She had been feeling nauseous for a while and thinking back she had, during that time, found herself obsessively cleaning her apartment and habitually antiquing on the link. It suddenly made some sense.
“I’ve only known you a week or so. I couldn’t possibly involved.” Cracker hoped she was more that a few weeks along.
“The body begins to produce human chorionic gonadotropin about 5 or so days after the fertilised egg is attached to the uterine wall. The scan shows cell reproduction and growth at about 7 to 10 days. The timings don’t seem to fit exactly, but they are within range for human development. Cracker, I don’t think I can’t defend you on this one.” Kathy Logan took off her patch and sighed. “This is going to mess up my buzz, mate.”
“No, No. Wait. I did not touch you. How do you know it wasn’t Johnny-boy?” Cracker was desperate. 
“He was injured and unconscious.” Sarah spat vitriol back at him.
“Well ladies and gentlemen, there appears to be another contender for father of the year. How will we get to the bottom of this little conundrum? If only there was a way to find out who the father is. Oh that’s right, I have a DNA-sequencer. I will just have to get a small sample and we will have an answer.” Kathy was feeling better now and slipped the patch back on. Her money was on the other creep, whoever he was. She knew Cracker and he was not that type. He could have taken advantage of her on any number of occasions, but had never crossed that line. Cracker was an enigma to Dr Logan, a paradox of amoral criminality and Victorian decency. “Just a quick jab, Sarah.”
The sequencer was loaded with the unborn child’s tissue sample and set to chug away for about 10 minutes as it checked, re-checked and checked the data again. 
“This is really weird, I mean really weird.” She could not hold back a hysterical laugh. “So strange. Only you could bring me something like this, Cracker.”
Kathy’s amusement did not reduce Cracker’s anxiety. His heart was pounding loudly and hot flushes pulsed across his body, leaving his face and neck a blotchy bright red. He wondered whether he had suffered from some memory lapse or had indulged in some form of sleep-fucking. Sleep-fucking? Is that a thing? He knew their way no way he was involved in the conception, but he was still petrified. He held his breath, crossed his fingers and hoped.
“Cracker, you are not the father.” 
“Thank the Dawkins.” Cracker blurted out, not knowing why. “Hell yeah! I told you, Sarah.” He raised both arms jubilantly and immediately regretted the little act of celebratory anger, but did not think to apologise.
“Well, you are hooked into the data-base, who is the father?” Sarah could not yet bring herself to believe the result. She had found it very easy to blame Cracker, but was finding extreme difficulty in withdrawing the accusation. Her womanhood had been assailed at its very core and the sick feeling of violation would not retreat.
 
“I can’t tell you that either. What I can tell you Sarah is that you are not the mother.” Kathy was enjoying herself, she loved when a mystery presented itself.
_ _ _
</Text>
        </Document>
        <Document ID="753D8A73-CE7B-4DC2-9ACB-029788579460">
            <Title>Search for the Rosetta Rock</Title>
            <Text>Search for the Rosetta Rock

The Johnny had hardly lifted his head from his work since Sarah had laid down the law 2 months prior. He had resolved to hunker down and produce results before turning his mind to revenge. He would do as he was told and keep complaints to a minimum. He calculated a total absence of complaints would be noticed, so he would throw in a few here an there just to keep in character. He even managed to talk Dr Kathy into hiring a cryptologist, a mathematician, an Egyptologist, several varieties of physicists and and a few other boffins to his team of techs and accelerate the analysis. Although he was too self-absorbed to notice, the improved work ethic lead to actual efficiency, productivity and a degree of work place harmony. His underlings didn’t even want to kill him anymore. A decent maiming would more than suffice. 

Sarah and Dr Kathy had been a little distracted in recent weeks, with the poison-attack on the Elvi and related security concerns for Richard, they had not blessed him with their presence. With the imminent completion of the private residences Sarah, Richard and Dr Kathy were moving in at the end of the week. The remote location and high security of the facility made it a perfect site to ensure young Richard’s safety. Upon arrival, no doubt, they would expect a progress report that chronicled actual progress and he was confident his news would would not displease.

Eight weeks of hard slog by the entire team had confirmed the markings in the Beta-mode identifier pattern were indeed some sort of message. The oscillations in the blurred marking were not random but patterns repeated in parallel lines, many times over. Initially, it was hoped the message would be found in the manner of repetition, not unlike some heavenly Morse code, but those hopes were soon dashed. Simplistic thinking would not crack this code.

“Could it be a musical scale?” Asked Senior Technical Officer Vilnius Cambridge at the daily briefing. A hail of notebooks and palm devices bounced off his forehead. 

“We’ve tried that.” The Johnny said.

“What about a logarithmic scale?” Vilnius replied.

“Give the music scales a break will you?” For the moment Johnny kept his cool.

“Well, we’ve got all the computer processing power in the world, making a billion calculations a second and for the last 2 months we have made virtually no progress.”

“I think it has something to do with gas chromatography.” Said the physicist, Rosalind Frankland. 

“No, light spectroscopy.” Argued the resident astrophysicist.

“Have either of you constructed a viable method of testing?” The Johnny asked.

“No.” They both replied. 

“The Egyptian Hieroglyphs were thought meaningless until the discovery of the Rosetta Stone.” Egyptologist added.

“Thanks for the history lesson, but how does that help?” The Johnny asked.

“Perhaps we need a cypher key or code phrase.”

“Okay, I’ll order one today.” The Johnny snapped back. “Problem solved.”

“For the translation we wish to make, there is no telling what the equivalent of a Rosetta Stone is, but if it can be identified, the message will translate itself.”

“So what you are saying is, we are searching for that elusive clue that will unlock the mystery?” The Johnny managed to remain calm. 
“Yes.”

“So how does that differ from what we are already doing?” The Johnny screamed at the history buff. “We are going to solve this with hard work, trial and error, plenty of error and some luck. Let’s get to it.”

The next morning the senior management team met as usual for the morning briefing. Vilnius Cambridge was nursing a few cuts and bruises, courtesy of yesterday’s briefing and had resolved to remain silent. Particle Physicist, Dr Bradley Quark, was fidgeting and could not wait for The Johnny to open the meeting. “I have been working on imaging. At ultra microscopic level the message have thousands of parallel markings with blurred, but delineated micro-grooves, sort of like a recording on those old black dics.”

“Like they used to record music on” Vilnius felt vindicated until the first notepad struck the bridge of his nose. He managed to duck the rest.

“You see people, our physicist has made an interesting observation. It may amount to nothing, but it is worth following up.” Johnny winced. He was not used to praising anyone, apart from himself. “Much better than Rosetta stone platitudes.””

“I’ve got more news.” The physicist said. “The images are blurred because they are slightly out of phase. If as you claim this is message is from before the big bang, I thought it may be from another universe, a universe where the universal gravitational constant is different.” 

“There are 26 fundamental constants that describe the universe, how did you decide upon the gravitational constant?”

“The discs are said to operate on gravity waves, I just figured it was a good starting point. I just got lucky.” The physicist admitted. 

“How lucky?” The Johnny was actually interested.

“I have only had time to do a quick analysis of two messages, but there are some interesting findings.” He switch on the holo-screen and pointed to an equation floating in the space before them. “As you know the universal gravitational constant is expressed by …….
#


……I filtered the images through a phase variance compensator and I have calculated, from the degree of variance, this message is from a universe with a slightly higher universal gravitational constant. When I tried to replicate the process with another message, I found the phase variance was different again, with the Universal Gravitational constant slightly lower than our universe.”

“Good work, doctor.” The Johnny tried to be cool but he was reeling. Different universes! “Congratulations, Dr Quark. We can actually report some real progress. How long until you can examine all of the messages?

“Well, if we share the load equally, we should only have 500 or 600 each to examine. If we can get more two more phase variance compensators, we should be finished before the end of the month.” Dr Quark replied.

“Excellent.” The Johnny stood and leaned across the table, offering his hand to Dr Quark. The Doctor took it hesitantly, but firmly and glanced at his colleagues, each of whom wore jaws agape. “You have made my day.”

“Thank you, Johnny” Dr Quark replied. The Johnny halted the handshake, mid-pump. 

“What of the other 25 universal constants? The fine structure constant? The strong coupling constant? Neutrino mixing Parameters? Quark Mixing parameters?” The Johnny stopped at that one. He saw a few of the lab coats chuckle. You don’t get to call me Johnny. 

“I am well aware of the quark mixing parameters.” Dr Quark sighed. He had had his fill of quark jokes. “I have not been able to cast my mind to the other constants, but my impression is they are probably not too different. Also, I would think if gravity is different in the other universes, time may also pass at a different rate.”

“When you have checked all of the messages, start on the other universal constants and get back to me.” The Johnny left the room without another word.

 
 - - -


The Elvis Security Teams descended on the facility 2 weeks prior to Sarah’s expected arrival and augmented the high security facility with state of the art automated defence systems, courtesy of Eloise Shakti. The entire complex was swept for bombs, booby-traps, weapons, listening devices, secret cameras and tin cans with lengths of string between them. Satisfied all was secure the interior designers were summoned, Elvi all, and took to the task of turning the sterile canvas into a warm, inviting home. Desperate to satisfy the needs of the fast growing Richard, each decision was debated, argued, altered, changed back and the cause of much pain. Surprisingly, the result was a beautiful and tasteful interior with light pastels contrasting the furnishing and ornate trim work. To everyone’s surprise it filtered through that Alexander Shakti was to join Sarah and Richard at the facility. According to the scuttlebutt he had arranged for time away from the office to finalise his report on Director ??? Murder. 

Sarah and Richard, especially Richard, were ecstatic with their new home. Sarah had resigned herself to something similar to upmarket camping, but the residence was spacious and included with every domestic device imaginable - devices to make easy tasks easier, but with proportionally crappier results. There was, however, no time for home making and Sarah arranged a meeting with The Johnny and Dr Kathy to get the first update she had received in a couple of weeks. She left Shakti to his complaints about how hard reports were to write and headed for her meeting. She had seen how hard he had been working, reading and re-reading transcripts, examining financial statements, computer activity and communication logs. She had offered assistance that he no doubt needed, but he had been determined to solve this one on his own, but was yet to identify a suspect.

Sarah walked briskly and confidently into the conference room, Richard bouncing off her hip and holding on tight. 

“Does he have to be here?” The Johnny asked. “Don’t let him touch anything.”

“Richard never leaves my side.” Sarah reminded him as she place her boy on the floor. Richard scooted across the floor to the nearest Elvi and begged to be picked up. The lucky Elvis gladly obliged.

“I was talking about Shakti.” Laughter filler the room. Even Sarah and Richard had a good chuckle at that one. 

“You are in a good mood, aren’t you?” Sarah joined Dr Kathy and The Johnny at the table.

“What about the Brylcreem security team?” The Johnny asked. “Do they have to stay?”

“You try to get them to leave.” Sarah challenged. “What do you think Team Leader?”

“Anyone interfering with our sacred task of protecting the great one will be neutralised.” Team Leader Elvis replied without hesitation. 

“”Let’s get started shall we?” Dr Kathy Logan was keen to get this over and done with and get on to the serious task of getting fucked up. “Johnny? Can you give us an update?”

“I have some marvelous news.” The Johnny smiled broadly and ran his finger across the pink cicatrice on his skull. “We have confirmed that the pattern is comprised of messages, multiple separate message from multiple alternate universes.”

The room was silent for an eternity until Richard started laughing loudly and clapping his hands madly. Sarah joined in, as did Kathy and the Security Team. Sarah felt a pure happiness beaming from Richard’s little chest and could not help but join in. It was clear Richard understood the implications of what had been said and he too thought it was marvelous.

“If you want to check the figures, I think you will confirm my results.” The Johnny wasn’t expecting laughter. 

Sarah laughed, not in disbelief, but in the sheer joy of a scientific discovery of this magnitude and of course the fact that everyone else laughed, making it even funnier. Confirming the multi-verse theory, or perhaps the big bang-big crunch theory, was a significant leap forward. 

“I believe you!” Sarah sputtered out

“When you examine the details in the report you will see that Dr Quark identified the messages each originated from places with different values for the Universal Gravitational Constant. Multiple alternate universes!”

“What of the messages themselves?” Dr Kathy asked, finally able to speak after the gob-smacking and for some reason funny news she had just heard. 

“We are no closer to translating, but Dr Quark discovered, just this morning, fundamental particles also have a slightly different electron volt values, except for the Higgs Boson. We don’t know, yet, if it will assist us in any practical way.”

The remainder of the meeting was spent on menial, but vital, arrangements relating to rostering, office supplies, overtime (there would be none) personal protective equipment, radiation shielding for food supplies. Shakti was to remain in the residential wing, unless accompanied by an adult. 

Richard took his first steps inside the residence and unlike his father, soon had the run of the entire complex. Sarah quickly gave up chasing him and left it to the security teams and nannies to keep him under control. He had the knack of teetering in on important meetings and most particularly, when The Johnny was conducting an experiments in the laboratory wing. Richard was always under foot, but never in the way and The Johnny, much to his chagrin, had to privately admit the child was very bright. Yet to say a word, Richard would smile when he heard something he liked, would frown for anything to his disliked and would cry if he disagreed or needed his nappy changed. He soon had the scientists well trained and taking instructions, his delightful disposition unable to be resisted. The team had to admit the little upstart had been right on every occasion he had intervened with a tantrum, which would not stop until a decision or nappy was changed. Sometimes both.

Security teams were perpetually on alert keeping up with the little dynamo, but none could think of anything more worthwhile to do with their lives than keeping him safe. There was nothing random in the nature of Richard’s wanderings and once he had sufficient gross motor function he began to run everywhere. Firstly he fell and tripped and screamed in frustration, too impatient to await fine motor  function in his feet and toes to catch up, but after many falls he finally began to run. He ran and ran, but not for the sake of running. Any objective observer would conclude he was training and when his upper body strength started to kick in, he confirmed this by commencing a regimen of push ups and arm curls. It did not go unnoticed that he was developing fast, very fast and grew noticeably larger by the day. It was calculated by one of the more inquisitive minds in the team that Richard was growing at 5 times the rate of an average child. This came as no surprise, Richard was anything but average. Initially there was some degree of concern that Richard’s cognition could not keep pace with the physical development, but his astonishing mind easily maintained the pace.

He was sneaky as he was smart and quickly learned to ditch his security teams and was forever being located in obscure nooks and crannies, somehow managing to defeat the security grid. On more than one occasion he has found in the test bunker examining the markings burnt into the concrete ceiling and walls of the vast empty space. Against the advice of the Elvi Security themselves, Sarah rejected calls to have him locked down with his dad. Apart from the cruel nature of such close proximity with Shakti, she thought there must be a reason for his infant-reconnoiters and suggested the Elvi should get on with doing their job. 

- - - 

The Elvi War Cabinet had again been called together for an emergency session to debate possible action in response to the genocide attempt by the PTD. Anger of the entire Elvi nation was focused the CEO and the Directorate of Proactive Euthanasia and Pre-emptive Reciprocity. The Elvi were ready to heat up this cold war.

“We have been very lucky.” Said the Minister of Health. “Not one death. We must be very grateful to the Blessed Mother and the protection of the Hybrid T-Virus. Many are still gravely ill, but seem to be recovering.”

“The lack of deaths does not reduce their culpability!” Reminded the Justice Minister. “Their intent was clear. Annihilation of us all.”

“We have already struck back at the PTD.” The High Elvis announced, “The Blessed Mother, some little time ago attacked them on our behalf and has caused significant damage. Financial losses are now only rippling through the economy. She has reduced the total wealth of the PTD by 20% and increased our holdings by 500%. Many of our most ardent enemies have been financially ruined. We have reports that the CEO himself is close to bankruptcy and desperate for funds.” 

“They must pay with their lives.” The Minister of War called out from across the table. “We have negotiated contracts to purchase arms from our saviour’s grandmother. All next generation firepower. They will have nothing the match us.”

“Until she sells the PTD the same weaponry.” Cracker, the Great Teacher, pointed out. “She may be an ally, but a sale is a sale. There are few things more important to the powerful than the bottom line.”

“We have plans in place, we have the weapons and we have the will.” The Minister of war barked back.

“And what do we do after we win?” The High Elvis posed. “I don’t want to preside over the PTD. Do you? That is a nightmare I wish to avoid. I am only interested in promoting our interests and our culture. It is far better to hit them where is hurts - in the pocket book.”

“What of the CEO?” The Minister for War wanted some blood to be spilt. He deserves more than mere poverty.”

“The CEO must answer to the Board of Directors. With the recent spate of bankruptcies the membership of the board has changed considerably and I am assured the majority are sympathetic to our cause.  Indeed, some of them are out largest investors. An insolvent CEO will never be allowed to continue.”

“You are mistaken, High Elvis. For the ultra-wealthy, bankruptcy is a momentary inconvenience.” Holy Aunt Hayley joined in. She knew how slippery her people could be. “We will need much more than a lack of liquidity to bring him down. Someone will make a deal, prop him up financially and have themselves a puppet. No, we will need to be something the elites will not forgive.”

“Do we know who his replacement might be?” The Minister of War was not convinced. “Better the devil you know.”

“It is my fondest hope it will be Eloise Shakti.” The High Elvis said proudly. “She may not be Elvis, but she will do anything to protect our saviour. I expect she will act in self interest, until in conflicts with her vow to protect Richard.”

“I agree, up to a certain point. I am willing to bet she has her price.” The Great Teacher suggested. “I propose no action be taken until the next meeting of the Board of Directors. There is no need for war.”

“I agree.” Holy Aunt Hayley said. 

“We vote.” The High Elvis said.

The vote was close, but The Great Teacher and the Holy Aunt managed to keep the peace in the PTD, at least in the short term. The meeting was adjourned and they all went out for cocktails and a show. After siphoning alcohol at an alarming rate over several hours, a drunken Great Teacher staggered away from the Quarter and slowly traversed half the city to his palace inside Hardy Tower 1. He did not notice the two well dressed goons following.

- - -


The Jacobson-Shakti clan had settled into a routine and quickly began to resemble an average, level 5, dysfunctional family. Both parents worked hard or at least one of them worked hard and Shakti wasted a ton of time staring at files not understanding a thing. The level 5 progeny, in the traditional fashion, was largely left to his own devices and spent his time training and studying every educational data base he could stream. He was not permitted to get his hands on a brain-dump set, one task the Elvi had not failed in, and had embraced reading books, both electronic and hardbacks. 

He firstly taught himself to read and then took on simple high school level material, but soon was devouring university texts. In a few weeks, while dad struggled to add two and two, the mute genius amassed the equivalent knowledge of doctorates in Quantum Physics, Mathematics and Biology.

Similarly, a routine had broken out throughout the complex. There was an air of optimism within the research team and each knew if they stuck to their tasks and crunch the numbers, they would succeed. Fame and fortune would surely follow. With the unexpected outbreak of harmony, Sarah found she had a some time on her hands and decided to interrupt Richard’s self-education and get in some quality time. She thought he would enjoy the simple pleasure of playing with brightly coloured toys and stuffed bears, but Richard had no interest in things puerile and simply wandered off, leaving mum to her toys.

“That went well.” Sarah sighed as she got up off the floor. She had figured she would become an embarrassment to her son when he was 14, not 14 months. She then caught a glimpse of Shakti’s open files hovering above his desk as the holo-emitter softly hummed. Shakti had worked all night again and would be asleep for many hours. She sat down and began to read, jumping artfully from data base to data base and by cross matching the finance and communication records, she was soon shaking her head in disbelief. The suspect was clear and she only needed to reconstruct a deleted video file and she would have the case wrapped up. Reconstructing dead files was something of which she had gained considerable experience when tracking down Emile Kalheri and she soon turned white noise into high definition holo-vid. She had to admit, Shakti had done a great job of collecting the evidence, all of the information was there, someone just had to take a look. A proper look.

“Alexander?” Sarah asked Shakti over afternoon tea. “With all of that information you have, do you have any suspects?”

“Yes, but I don’t want to say. You will think it is stupid.” Shakti said, hoping she would not press for an answer.

“Tell me, please.” Sarah said, taking a dainty sip of tea.

“Alright. Promise you won’t laugh.” He waited until she nodded. “The CEO.”

Sarah spat her tea back into her cup, coughing and spluttering. He actually worked it out!

 “I asked you not to laugh.”

“I’m not laughing. I believe you, trust me.” She then made a call the the Commissioner’s office. 


- - -

“Good Morning Commissioner.” A cheerful Sarah said on being connected.

“Hi, Sarah. How can I help you today?” Commissioner Hayley Lanning, the Holy Aunt, was pleased to hear from Sarah. There had been nothing but good news since she finally took over the lab facilities and Hayley was happy to plough more resources into the operation. “Any problems with Johnny?”

“No, everything seems to running smoothly here and they are making progress every day. I am actually calling about Alex.”

“Who?”

“Shakti.”

“Yes, of course. Has he finished that report yet? It’s months overdue.” Hayley dropped into Commissioner mode.

“He thinks the CEO was behind it and I think he’s right.”

“Don’t be absurd.”

“No, but I had a good look at the date and did a little digging and was able to raise a deleted communications file and security files.” Sarah paused for a moment. “It is the entire call between the CEO and Director ??? It records the murder and it is clear the CEO directing the events. I am sending you the file now.”

Instantaneously a hologram of the CEO and Director ??? formed above Hayley’s desk. The hologram of the CEO was hovering above the CEO’s desk when the Office Manager burst in and fired one clean shot to the forehead of the Director, killing him instantly. Within a few moments, the Office Manager had placed the gun barrel to her temple and fired without hesitation. “Excellent” the floating head commented and then disappeared only to return a few minutes later claiming he knew not what had happened. There was no doubt the CEO was behind the murder of Director XXXX and the death of the office manager.

“Well, it looks like we have our man and this is very timely indeed.”

“No.” Sarah said. “Lieutenant Alexander Shakti has his man.”

“Sarah, he can’t be involved in this, now. It’s too important.” 

“Just let him do the arrest. You will be there to hold his hand, but let him take the credit.” Sarah earnestly felt Shakti deserve a break. “Don’t let him speak to the press, he’s hopeless without a cue-cards.”

“Okay, he gets to say ‘you’re under arrest’ and that is it.” Hayley countered. “Does he know he’s cracked the case yet?”

“No, I will go through it with him now.” Sarah knew explaining it to him would take some significant time. “I’ll send him over tomorrow morning and you can make your plans.”

“Okay. I expect to see Shakti in my office at 7.00am tomorrow.” Hayley said. “I think we will drop in on the Board of Directors meeting.”

“Maximise his embarrassment?” Sarah asked.

“You got it.”


_ _ _ 

Cracker approached loading dock 20, located at the rear of Hardy Tower 1, but prior to entry he made one last glance around to ensure he had not been followed. He entered the dock and approached a non-descript lightly painted brick wall that, upon his approach, began to shimmer before revealing itself as an elevator door which automatically opened. As the door slid open Cracker was picked and hurled into the elevator by two darkly dressed and serious looking dudes. 

“Hey! What the fuck fellas?” Cracker queried. 

“Shut the fuck up little man.” The taller of the two said. ‘What floor are we headed for?” 

“Top floor, but the controls will not work for you.” Cracker replied. “Let me do it.” Cracker rose to his feet and waived his hand in the general direction of what appeared to be a control panel and the elevator immediately shot skyward for the 210 floor trip to his penthouse. He was then struck on the back of the head and stumbled forward. “Ouch! What was that for, mate? I may be drunk but I am still feelin’ pain.” 

“Yeah, bullshit.” Said the shorter but quite obviously stronger man who then delivered a punch that would have sent any heavyweight over the ropes to land unconscious in the third row. The blow barely knocked Cracker backwards more than a few steps. Unperturbed another blow of equal might landed on Cracker’s nose, causing little damage and no bleeding.

“Ouch! Dude, Dude…It’s not going to work.” Cracker said softly, raising both hands. “Let’s just go upstairs and have a beer, you know, like civilized men.”

“We have our orders.” Said the strongman.

“Well, let’s see if we can accommodate them, huh?” Cracker smiled back as the two men exchanged perplexed glances. “If you are going to try and kill me, I’ve been killed before. Live on the link.”

“Was that you?” The tall one smiled. “How did you survive?”

“Long story, but I can assure you, those PPP’s you have under your jackets will do you no good.” Cracker replied. “I’ve been tortured by one of the best in the business and he failed to get me to talk. So, boys, I am happy to discuss anything you want, but try and coerce me and I you will get nothing.”

The elevator door slid open revealing the luxuriant squatters apartment Cracker had claimed as his own. The darkly dressed mercinaries were simply gob-smacked by the decadence of the atrium.

“Welcome to my humble abode, gentlemen.” Cracker laughed and knew from their faces they had never seen anything like the opulence laid out before them. “So then, what do you fuckers want?”

“We know that this was the site where the massive cyber-attack on the financial system was launched.” Tall guy said. 

“What are you the fuckin’ police or something?”

“No, we are representing private interests.”

“Sounds like someone wants in on the action.” Cracker countered.

“More like our client wants to protect the finance system from the likes of you. The attack has caused untold anguish to many prominent citizens”

“Their anguish is nothing compared to the pain those arseholes have caused, just by their existence.” Cracker said. A fist again struck his face with tremendous force and a loud smack. “Stop it! That fuckin’ hurts. I was not the author of the attack, I don’t know how the system work.”

“Who knows?” The tall guy seemed to be in charge.

“I will have to make a call. Is that okay?” Cracker hoped it would be.

“Yes, but put it on speaker and if you say anything to give us away, I ‘ll do my very best to tear your fucking head off and we’ll see if you can survive that.” 

Cracker pulled out his hand device and made the call.

“Cracker, do you know what time it is?” Sarah said. “Voice only? Why no vid?”

“I’m on the shitter.”

“Thanks for that.” Sarah sighed. “What’s so urgent?”

“Look, I was in the control centre earlier and I think there is something wrong with the data base.”

“How so?”

“It’s beeping constantly” Cracker lied. “It sounds like an alarm and I thought it might have something to do with the last time we used the system. You know.”

“Yes, that does sound a little odd, but I can’t leave at the moment. My boy is sleeping.”

“Yes, Jonesy needs his sleep, but I really think this needs your immediate attention.” Cracker replied. 

“You sound strange. Are you drunk?”

“Yeah, a little, but I am sobering up fast.” 

“You should not be messing with that system when you have been drinking.” Sarah warned. “I can come over in the morning.”

“Okay, can you tell me how it works? I am going to have a look at it myself.” Cracker said.

“No, you mustn’t.” Sarah said, concern creeping into her voice. “Okay, I will be there as soon as I can arrange a shuttle. Three quarters of an hour?”

“Sounds good.” Cracker said. “Don’t bring little Jonesy with you.” He terminated the call before she could answer.


 - - - 


“Jonesy?” Sarah had no idea what Cracker meant. It was now 5.30am and upon dressing she went to the kitchen and saw Shakti at the dining table making preparations for his big day. His first big arrest.

“It looks like there’s even more to do after an arrest.” Shakti said. “Who would have thought?”

“I have to go to the business district for a quick meeting with Cracker.” Sarah announced.

“This early? It must be important.”

“I don’t know, actually.” Sarah replied. “He called Richard, Jonesy. Very odd.”

“What, like that murdering Agent friend of yours?”

“He was never a friend! He tortured Cracker.” Sarah shot back. “…he tortured Cracker….” She grabbed her palm device from her pocket and had the Head of Elvi Security on the screen in seconds. “Get a team together.”

Richard appeared from his bedroom and upon seeing his mother raised his hands, demanding to be picked up. Dutifully, Sarah obliged and wedged him on her right hip.

“Good morning my little genius. Mummy is going on an errand today and you will have to stay at home.” Sarah explained. “It might be dangerous.”

Richard grabbed on tight and would not let go and then he began to cry. And cry. He bellowed even louder when Shakti tried, once only, to dislodge him. He would not budge.

_ _ _

The elevator raced toward the Penthouse, Richard happily on the floor, front and centre of the elevator. He resisted his mother and any Elvi that attempted to raise him off the ground. Sarah could feel he actually wanted to be the first out of the elevator and when she made attempts to pick him up he would scream, killing any chance of a stealthy entry into the penthouse atrium.  As the elevator approached its destination the rate of ascent slowed considerably. The Elvi Security Team did a final weapons check and attempted to step forward when Richard stiffened both arms and raised them sideways to the horizontal with his palms backwards. Sarah and each member of the team were frozen in place.

“Richard.” Sarah whispered. “Please, darling.”

“It will be alright, mother.” Richard said. 

“I’m begging you, please.” Sarah breathlessly pleaded, tears coursing out of the corner of each eye. When the shock of his first words began to sink in, Sarah did not know what was more surprising, the fact that Richard could speak perfectly well or that he spoke in a regal English accent. 

As the doors slid open, Sarah’s mind was wild with desperate thoughts of protecting her young boy. There could, very well be nothing untoward awaiting them, but her good sense told her something else. 

Cracker stood three or four decent strides in front of the elevator and stiffened with genuine surprise when Richard stepped off the elevator alone. He could see Sarah and the security team standing mute and motionless at the back of the car and could not fathom why.

“Jonesy?” Cracker managed to spit out.

Richard smiled brightly and ran towards Cracker, but stopped short and turned around to see two goons standing either side of the elevator door pointing their PPP’s directly at him. 

“There is a hole in your shoe.” Richard said politely and then turned to Cracker, arms raised. The two gunman shrugged shoulders and shot each other in the foot.

 “You can speak?” Cracker held him tight as he saw Sarah and the security detail pour out of the elevator and secure the two men writhing on the floor, each grasping a slippery red shoe.

“Yes, Great Teacher.” Richard said with a wry smile. “May I call you Great Teacher? I think Cracker Hardy is a little too childish for a grown man. Don’t you think?”

“Whatever you say little buddy.” Cracker was filled with joy and wondered, momentarily, what having a child of his own might be like. Nah, I’d fuck it up. His train of thought was disrupted by Sarah reefing Richard out of his arms and hugging him tightly. She began to sob loudly.

“Don’t you ever do that to me again.” Sarah she wailed. “Do you hear me? You are more important than anyone. That includes me and in definitely includes Cracker!”

“Mother, dear. I love you and The Great Teacher, but I did not do this for either of you.” Richard said. “I did it for them.” He pointed to two Elvi restraining one of the prisoners. “They would have been shot in the head as soon as they stepped off the elevator. They were expecting a woman to step off out and as soon as they saw two men they would have opened fire. They, of course would have been killed by the rest of our team and I could not allow that either.”

“Who cares about those criminals?” Sarah asked, her sobs dying down.

“I do. People, like species, should be allowed to evolve and this experience will give them much to reflect upon.”

“How did you know what would happen?” Sarah inquired.

“I saw it happen.” Richard said with a degree of certainty the great sage Kleo would have deemed hubris. “I can’t explain it to you right now, but time is more flexible than you think. What we should do is find out who sent these men here.”

“Are you trying to take over?” Sarah said jabbing him lightly in the chest. “Yes you are. Aren’t you? You are so cute. She cuddled him close, her face beaming. “Team Leader? Interrogate those men and find out who sent them.”

“Mother dear, stop that.” Richard began squirming. “Mother, put me down. Please.” Sarah place him down and he scurried off towards the interrogation. 

 “So cute.”

“When did he start to talk?” Cracker asked.

“He just started in the elevator.”

“Precocious little fucker.” Cracker laughed. “Just look at him.”

Richard approached the Elvi who all bowed reverently. “May I speak to them, team leader?”

“Of course Great One” The team leader said. “We are here to serve.”

“You chaps look a little unhappy.” Richard turned to the team leader. “Those shoes don’t match, do they?”

“What? What are you crapping on about kid?”

“Well, your shoes don’t match and it is offending my sense of symmetry. I was wondering if you would like a hole in the other shoe, that’s all.”

“No!” The prisoner cried. 

“Well then, why don’t you tell us who hired you.” The little man smiled.

“We will be killed.”

“They will probably kill you anyway, but if you help us, you will be protected.” Richard pointed out.

“Our client is more powerful that you can imagine.”

“I am personally protected by the Elvi Nation with the backing of my grandmother, Eloise Shakti.” 

Both prisoners burst into laughter and could not stop. Richard was a little shaken, they laughed at the might of the Elvi, armed with the latest firepower. 

“Okay, What’s so funny?”

“You’re protected by Eloise Shakti?” The second prisoner continued to cackle. “She’s our client!” The prisoners writhed on the floor giggling, until the gunshot wounds stopped them.

“Mother?” Richard called out. “Mother, I think we have a problem.”

Bored Meeting 

“It is good to see new board members taking up their positions. New blood and new ideas will be needed for the challenges ahead.” The CEO said, opening the annual board meeting. “As you know there has been a schism, for want of a better word, in the finance system which has caused a temporary reduction in expected revenue.”

“Yes, Mr CEO, some of our most prominent citizens are bankrupt.” Eloise Shakti teased. “How have your fared in these hard times?”

“My portfolios is intact.” The CEO lied, precipitating muted, bemused laughter from the board members. 

“This schism, as you call it, was a deliberate attack upon the finances of the top 1% of the Dominion.” Eloise said. “I have had my forensic accountants looking at it for weeks. The Elvi Nation’s investments and holding improved by 500% in a few hours. I was lucky enough to have some investments with them, along with a few of our colleagues here. Without these investments, I would be bankrupt, just like you Mr CEO.” A few surprised looks and cries of shock rumbled around the giant conference table, however there were a few who were not surprised and sat, knowingly, in stoney silence.

“How dare you?” The CEO stood to his feet and stared down Eloise. “That is an outrageous allegation. Where is your proof? I don’t care who you think you are, but you will not survive this meeting unless you have proof.”

“Every member of this board is aware your debts have been called in, you have taken out bridging finance with all sorts of predatory lenders. You are drowning in debt and I, as a member of the Board of Directors of the Primary Trade Dominion, are demanding you prove your liquidity or you will be removed from the board.”

“I do not answer to you”

“You answer to the board.” Eloise looked to her Boardroom Colleagues who were all nodding in agreement. 

At moment the giant double doors of the board room creaked opened, revealing the Commissioner of Police, Hayley Lanning and Lieutenant Shakti awaiting entry.

“What is this?” The CEO roared. “Commissioner you have no business here.”

“Yes she does.” Lieutenant Shakti stepped forward, into the room, and took a direct line to the CEO and trunig his head his head to Hayley Lanning. “Now?”

“Not yet.” Hayley rolled her eyes.

THIS IS WHERE ELOISE INTRODUCES DAMIEN HARDMAN AND TELLS THEN HE IS HER OPERATIVE.

“Ichabod Carmichael Wallington-Smythe. You are under arrest for the murder of Director XXXX of the Department of Pre-emptive Reciprocity and Pro-active Euthanasia. You are not obliged to say anything unless you wish, as anything you say will be recorded and may be used in evidence. Do you understand that?”   
“The only thing I understand is that I am looking at two ex-police officers. I am immune from prosecution.”

“Cue the holo-vid.” Eloise called out. “Let’s see how long that immunity lasts.”

“You are in on this?” The CEO asked Eloise. 

“We are all here to see your demise” said Eloise as a holo-vid hovered above the boardroom table. The CEO’s culpability in the death of Director XXXXXX was bared for all to see. There was no doubt he arranged the killing and in the ordinary course of events that would not have been enough to dislodge him from the CEO’s chair, but his weakened financial position undermined any thoughts of redemption. It was perfectly okay for him to be a murderer, most of the members of the board had ordered a killing or two in their time, but a bankrupt murderer? That was a bridge too far.

Eloise stood and looked around at her shocked colleagues, “Did you seek the authority of the board of directors before terminating Director……….. Contract?” 

The CEO stared here down but, wheezed out a feeble “No”.

“Then you have breached your contract and your immunity does not extend to acts in breach of contract.” Eloise took a quick look at each of member of the board. “I move that Ichabod Charmichael Wallington-Smythe, be removed as CEO. Do I have a second?”

“I second that”
“I second that”
“So do I”
“I call for a vote. A two-third’s majority will suffice.” Eloise announced. “A show of hands?” Immediately the right hand of every board member shot into the air. “Unanimous. Mr CEO, you are hereby terminated.”

Lieutenant Shakti and Commissioner Hayley Lanning took the CEO into custody and escorted him out of the room in silence.

“Was that your son?” said one of the newly minted board members.

“Shut up.” Eloise replied. “The next item on the agenda is the election of a new CEO.”



- - - 

</Text>
