        <Document ID="5AF4D6DF-933A-432A-A43D-DEE70BF3CD2D">
            <Title>Cancelled out discs</Title>
            <Text>Cancelled out Discs
The Johnny was buzzing, his hands clammy shaking from a cocktail of endorphins, adrenaline and grand ambition . His team had made a discovery of proportions unimagined. If he milked circumstance and misrepresented himself, his name would last forever. It had been an arduous task for his team, but they had completed the analysis of his last, impromptu and near disastrous experiment. The results were simply staggering. 
“Taking credit for this will be my greatest achievement.” He accidentally said out loud, instantly regretting his enthusiasm as his eyes darted about to confirm no-one had heard. The appointment with Sarah was only a few minutes away and he readied himself for the accolades that he would, no doubt, be buried in.
She arrived with an entourage of Elvi servants, all fussing over the One-after-the-One, Dr Kathy Logan and to his horror, Detective Chief Superintendent Hayley Lanning. He was pleased, however, that the ignoramus known to him as Cracker, was not among their number. 
“This had better be good.” Hayley let Johnny know she was in no mood for his self indulgent rot. She also had her fill of complaints from his team, all of whom claimed they were in imminent peril. It seemed not a day would go past without receiving a report of some petty outrage. He tried to kill me with a ray gun! She silently lampooned. They are lucky to have jobs. “I do not ordinarily leave the office at the caprice of junior contractors, so get ready to impress me.” She knew he would not, could not, let this insult slide and waited for his brain to explode. 
“Thank you for being so kind as to visit Superintendent.” The Johnny said, trying on a fake smile. Junior contractor? He knew he couldn’t pull off a real smile, but it only mattered that he held his temper long enough to claim the discovery as his own. “Your efforts will be worth it.” He continued, choking down his ego.
Superintendent Lanning found herself surprised and a little alarmed by his restraint. Whatever he had to announce, she opined, took precedence over his pride and must be very important indeed.
“What have you discovered?” Sarah also wanted to hear the news. 
“I ask that the room be cleared. Just Sarah, the good Superintendent and I will remain.”
“No, Kathy stays and Richard never leaves my sight.” Sarah was also confident Richard would make it known when The Johnny was fibbing and she would, somehow, understand. 
“Okay, the smart-arse kid gets to stay.” The Johnny immediately relented. “My experiment with centrifugal force upon the discs has yielded some interesting results. The spinning of both discs created a gravity well and our simulations confirm it would have grown, at an exponential rate, becoming a small black hole. The earth was at risk of being consumed before I managed to stop it.”
“This child stopped it, not you.” Dr Kathy snapped. Richard giggled with a big toothless grin and clapped his tiny hand together heartily. “It was all you, wasn’t it little man?” Kathy whispered in Richard’s ear as she tickled his soft little belly.
“That is not the way I remember it.” His could not process facts that challenged his self importance. “I draw your attention to the holo-screen you will notice images taken from the inside of the bunker. Burnt into the walls and ceiling are familiar patterns. Or are they? Looking closely you may notice that there is one extra line.”
“I would expect the pattern to be the same. Aren’t they supposed to be a representation of the gravity waves at the time of the big bang? Why would they change?” Sarah was confused, but intrigued.
“I have not worked that one out yet, but this is something that will interest you. You will note that the patterns appear to be a many short fuzzy, oscillating lines randomly placed, but all falling within a generally circular pattern. I have had my techs working night and day and I think they are visible representations of digital signals, coded messages, not random oscillations. And there are hundreds of them!”
“That is impossible.” Sarah stared off into space. “Messages from the time of the big bang?”
“Before the big bang.” The Johnny then took a deep breath. “Messages from God.”
“Again impossible.” Sarah reiterated. “And you cannot jump to that conclusion, there must be many equally valid explanations.” Sarah was dumbfounded, but could not readily think of another explanation. God cannot be the answer. It simply cannot be so, Sarah kept to herself.
‘Yes, Johnny, unless you want to be arrested, I would go easy on the God delusion.” Hayley warned. “In any case, what ever the markings mean to you is not particularly relevant, Johnny.” Hayley needed to bring him down a notch. “It seems a bit pointless if we don’t know what the messages say, if they are indeed messages.”
“We could be looking at signals from before the beginning of time.” The Johnny let weight of the announcement settle before continuing, “This could be the most important break-through in history. Or histories.”
“Well, if it is what you claim, I will ensure your team gets the credit.” Hayley would make certain Johnny received no accolades. 
“It’s my team! My discovery. My destiny!!” Johnny’s imagined Nobel Prize had been snatched away, just when it could be seen so clearly. “Did you at least bring the Anti-T virus innoculant? I need to continue my work.”
“Dr Logan has the innoculant, but slow down a bit. How long until you can confirm what they are? ” Hayley needed to take control. “I don’t want you doing any more tests until you have a reconstructed message or until I am satisfied they are not messages at all. If they are, they might give us some clues as to how to deal with these wretched discs.”
“I have my subordinates working on that problem.” Johnny countered “I am free to do what I want. My team, my….”
“No! Not your team, not your discovery, not your destiny. The department owns you and everything you do. I am the Director of this idiotic venture and you will do my bidding. If you do not pull yourself into line, I will terminate your contract and it will be agonising. Is that the what you want?”
“No, no it is not.”
“You risk becoming superfluous to need, so do as I say.” Hayley had made her point. “I did not want to do this, but it is clear you cannot be trusted. Sarah is now in charge of this entire complex, including all experiments and research. You will not do anything without her permission. Do you understand?” Supt Lanning berated.
“Yes.” Johnny looked defeated, but his ego would never allow him to submit. I will exact my revenge, I don’t care how long it takes, I will prevail! I didn’t make zero contribution for nothing!
“Good. Then I will leave you to it, Sarah. I have a promotion to suck up for.” Hayley bailed with neither a word nor glance.
“First order of business is your disregard for the command structure.” Sarah was looking at her notepad and started on her list. “You must submit your plans in advance. You must give weekly progress reports to the new formed oversight committee. Members of the committee are Dr Kathy Logan, PhD Level 5, Cracker Hardy, Venture Capitalist, L.2 and myself. We will decide what you may and may not do.”
“Cracker? Venture capitalist, are you kidding?” The Johnny was non-plussed. 
“He is going to come into a great deal of money shortly, enough to buy into any level, above you even. So yes, Cracker. Courtesy of Hayley’s peculiar sense of humour or, perhaps, sense of irony. Either way, he gets to tell you what to do.” Sarah’s smile was as large as the awful, jagged pink scar adorning the top of Johnny’s scalp. 
‘Secondly, I will be taking an office here and fitting out the admin-wing as a residence. At any given time at least one of the committee will be present and you will obey their instructions no matter what.”
“I understand.” Johnny was close to tears. 10 minutes prior he was clutching a Nobel Prize.
“It does not matter if you understand or or not. It does not matter if you agree or disagree. What matters is that you obey.” Sarah stared him down. “Johnny, do no delude yourself, you are about to have your contract terminated. Suspended only until your next mistake. I intend to keep you alive, even if you are intent on getting yourself killed.”
“Anything else?” Johnny had had enough.
“Yes. I want you to refrain from killing your colleagues. These techs are seriously intelligent and are valuable to the organisation.” 
“Oh, they exaggerate. A few Gamma rays never hurt anyone.” Johnny said without a skerrick of humour or sarcasm. “They are nothing, stuck at level 4, never to be elites.” 
“Dr Logan will stay until my return.” Sarah announced. “Kathy? Take custody of the discs and make sure they reconstruct the messages before planning anymore experiments. Do not inoculate disc B before they have a coherent explanation for their results.”
“Got it.” Kathy giggled. She had brought a month’s supply of patches and was all set. “I will set myself up in your office and get to it. You can move out with the rest of the lab-techs.” She was sharp enough to remove herself from the control room before Johnny registered his inevitable complaint.
* * * *********************************************************************************************
As much as he loved proximity to Sarah, Cracker had not joined her on the second trip to the lab, but arranged to meet her later that day in Jameson Hardy’s Operations Centre. He was still hopeful of accessing the riches Jameson had squirreled away those many years ago, but his knowledge of ancient computer code was minimal. Fucking up the entire system would be the inevitable result of his limited skill set clashing with the old-tech. Sarah was the only one who could help.
He had managed to find an alternate entrance to Jameson Hardy’s opulent apartment, avoiding the necessity and hassle of stealing past the heavy security of the exclusive Gravity Well Restaurant. Through an ordeal of trial and error, mostly error, over several weeks of late night jaunts, he blundered across the tycoon’s private elevator and now enjoyed easy access from street level. He had all but moved into the apartment, but found himself lonely among the finery. He had never felt lonely in the Pale, there was alway someone screaming or someone stabbing someone for screaming. For that reason he had always coveted solitude, but right now, solitude sucked dick. He wanted to show off his 7-star accommodations, he wanted to be one of those painful new-rich, unable to control ostentatious displays of wealth. One day soon. 
Although he was keen to remove every credit from the vast pile Jameson’s computers had collected, he had taken on board Sarah’s stark warning that messing nsequences to the world economy. She had been with the program may have dire colargely absent from Cracker’s world in the weeks leading up to the birth of Richard, but even with a fleeting glimpse of the data-base, she was certain the program controlled a significant chunk of the world debt. It was impossible to predict how, exactly, economies would falter and Sarah was reluctant to tinker and provoke a cascade of losses. In that eventuality the wealthy would, no doubt, throw a tantrum costing thousands, perhaps millions of lives. 
He entered the control room but, forbidden to touch anything, was immediately bored. He wandered aimlessly, opening and shutting doors of empty cabinets, pulling out drawers and rifling through the few items left behind. After only a few minutes he had pretty much exhausted all possible sticky-beaking opportunities and had one last door to open. As the final door creaked open, he entered a large, walk in cupboard containing every cleaning product any self respecting commercial cleaner would ever need. There was even an arcane mop and bucket, the utility of which was not lost on Cracker, long desperate to clear the multi-layered dust accumulated by time. He and the mop made their way around the floor with speed and expertise, replacing blackened water and chemical at regular intervals. 
He adeptly danced with the mop, gliding across the floor backwards swiping figure 8’s, each stroke slicing through the filth and unveiling hardwood of glowing Burgundy. He cleared wide swathes up and down the control room, glancing through the transparent doorways at every pass and noted “Gravity Well” had just started luncheon service. Lunch was elegantly chaotic, with unsmiling patrons waiting impatiently, neuroses on standby, for something worthy of complaint. Any misstep would see personality disorders flare up and contrive to destroy the dim-witted wait-staff. For some reason the inferior did not seem to comprehend or acknowledge their lowliness and needed regular reminders. Keep the common in their place and keep the company in the black.
Curious to take a closer look at the freak show unfolding before him, Cracker approached the second of the portals. Through it he could see that several waiters were on the receiving end of loud and intense abuse from various patrons. One waitress, it seemed, had been unable to predict what wine the patron wanted and was suffering from her lack of clairvoyance. These employees were no level 1 scum, either. To occupy the position of waiter in ‘Gravity Well’, one had to be at least level 3 and often as high as level 4. Even so, the executive classes looked upon them with an intensity of hate only wealthy hearts could generate. 
Perhaps it was his loneliness or his natural dislike of these prancing ponies but Cracker’s impulse control abandoned him. Without any particular plan, without even thinking, he found himself walking through the shimmering doorway and into the finest dining room on the planet. Three or four fast paced steps had him standing before a flabby level 6 executive.
“What the hell are you?” The bloater bellowed. “Where did you come from?”
“Cracker of the Hardy clan.” Cracker punched him in the face and watched as the bubble of lard flopped about on the floor, desperately trying to right himself. Security sprinted towards him, but Cracker was already headed for his private exit and the door was open and closed before anyone could intervene. 
Several perplexed guards and the matre‘d (?) bashed at the wall with their fists, but were met with solid stone. One security guard produced his P.P.P and let off a few pulses into the wall, but with no effect. The stone did not even chip, while on the other side, Cracker gave them a one finger salute, followed by a traditional and heart-felt brown-eye.
“What are you up to, Great Teacher?” said a voice from behind. 
“Teaching them a lesson.” Cracker turned to see the Blessed Mother with Richard wedged to her hip and a small team of Elvis guards following behind. “Good, you found the entrance. It wasn’t too hard to find I hope. No Blessed Aunt Kathy?” 
“No, she is trying to stop Johnny destroying the world. What is that all about?” She asked, looking through the doorway and into Gravity Well. “Are they shooting at us?” 
“Yeah, I guess they are.” 
“What did you do?” Asked Sarah, in the manner a dried up Headmistress might question a child, just prior to the beating.
“See fat-arse in the corner? The one spitting up teeth?” Cracker asked, not requiring an answer. “He was screaming at the poor waitress. It was terrible, so I popped him one.”
“That large gentleman I recognise as CFO of Primary Trade Dominion Gas and Oil.” She said before finding herself distracted by the fate of the waitress. “Nice work. It looks like she’s been fired. Security is marching her to the door.” Sarah pointed out. “You should act more prudently. Uninformed action, can have unexpected consequences.”
“Level 5’s and 6’s don’t have to control themselves. Why should I be expected to behave any better?” He said as he watched the waitress disappear. “Okay, yeah, I have buyer’s remorse. I will make it up to her, I promise.” He was yet to discover that rich men need not keep their promises. Making them was gift enough.
“That is why I expect better of you.” She replied. “You actually care, don’t you?”
“I guess that’s why I belted him.” Cracker said, “Well your visit is timely, Blessed Mother, I am expecting the High Elvis and his entourage. They wish to pay homage to Richard.”
“Yes, he contacted me a little while ago.” Sarah replied. “He is coming with his entire cabinet.”
“I knew I was having a couple of guests, but I didn’t know I was throwing a party.” Things are starting to look up.
“Well, what have you prepared for refreshments?” She looked about and shrugged her shoulders. “Nothing, I see.”
“I’ll just grab some fruit, although I won’t be having any today.” Cracker loved the fresh fruit, so much so he had made the unfortunate discovery that an exclusive diet of fruit turned his arse into a fire hose. “Yeah, I might stick with red wine and cheese, mostly cheese.” 
The High Elvis and his cabinet arrived and were ushered into the library wing and seated at a wooden table of ornately carved walnut. Sarah, Richard and her Elvi followed closely behind.
“Books! Books made of paper!” The Blessed Mother was shocked. “These books must be priceless. Look at them! Beautifully bound and gleaming. This is my idea of heaven.” Drawn to the shelves of neatly stacked hard backs of every kind, she opened books at random and nose-dived into the pages to deeply draw in the scent of printers ink and bleached paper. “They’ve never been opened! What a tragedy. No one have ever read them?”
“Take what you like.” Cracker kindly offered.
“You don’t actually own any of this, not yet anyway.” Sarah warned. “At the moment you are merely the most successful squatter in history.”
“Okay, I will keep them myself.” He did not know what he would use them for. Reading them certainly wasn’t high on the agenda. Door stop, perhaps? Fat Frisbee?
“Blessed Mother we have much to discuss, but first may I hold the great one?” The High Elvis asked, hoping not to be denied.
“Of Course,” Sarah handed over Richard, who kicked his legs about in delight.
“It is indeed a blessing to hold the One-after-the-One. All Hail our Saviour!” The High Elvis held the child aloft and the Cabinet bowed in silent adoration. “All hail The Dawkins.”
“Praise be unto him” The Elvis Cabinet sang out with pure joy. 
“What do you wish to discuss H.E.?” Sarah decided saying High Elvis all of the time was far too formal, especially for the Blessed Mother. 
“The celebration of the birth of our Saviour. The Elvi nation is still largely ignorant of his existence and this cannot continue. Only a lucky few know of the blessed event and even though we have managed to keep it from common knowledge, it cannot stand. I would argue that it shouldn’t. We must celebrate this wonderful news and it must be done very soon. The Elvi are not fools and must realise that the birth is long overdue.”
“I want the Elvi to have their celebration, too, but I do not want to place Richard in peril. The P.T.D. know of him, I mean there are several million ‘The one-after-the-one is coming’ posters glued to every building in the Pale. Elvis concerts have been replete with songs and monologues about ‘The Dawkins’ for many months and we know the P.T.D. are plotting to kill off the Elvi nation. How are you going to protect him, once his identity is known?”
“The first thing is to ensure his identity is not discovered, not until he is much older, but we must continue to spread his legend. He cannot be allowed to fade from memory. You and Richard will have, at your disposal, all the resources of the Elvi Nation. We do not have much capital to spare, much has been diverted to Graceland Security, but we have the man-power to guarantee your security indefinitely. Your current arrangements are temporary and we need a long term plan, preferably involving a clandestine safe-house.”
“I already have that covered.” Sarah said, thinking of her new Directorship at the Lab. “Yes, I have a bomb-proof bunker to hide in and the living quarters will be completed in a matter of weeks. We just need to survive until then. My concern is the P.T.D. identifying Richard as the One-after-the-One.”
“You could have called him something other than Richard-Dawkins.” The High Elvis noted with a touch of sarcasm. “I will make arrangements. We will leak some disinformation. A few red herrings here and there should thin out their resources.”
“I understand the Elvi deserve their prize. They have treated me with such kindness and respect and I will be forever grateful.” Sarah said. “I can’t stop you having a celebration, but I do not think Richard should be present. The CEO knows of Richard’s existence, but not his identity and has asked our friend Hayley, Holy Aunt Hayley, to hunt down the Saviour.”
“She won’t compromise his safety, will she?” H.E. was horrified at the prospect. Surely she will not turn on us so easily? “She is venerated in our community and the entire Elvis continuum would be deeply wounded if she placed Richard in peril.”
“If she misses out on the Commissioner’s job, there is no telling how she will react.” Sarah said with a note of dismay. “She is very much a career woman.”
 * * * * * * *
“We have a very strong field for this job, Superintendent.” The CEO announced. “We even have a Level 6 contender. The upper executive classes will need a very good reason to overlook him.”
“Raise my taxes and garnish my super! Why would a level 6 stoop so low?” Hayley thought it absurd that she coveted this job more than anything, but for a “sixer” it was a retrograde step. “He or she must have their reasons, but I have never known an altruistic upper executive.”
“Whatever the motivation, the application has been transmitted and is being processed like all of the others.” The CEO enjoyed making his junior executive squirm. “You can make your bid for the job by identifying this so-called Saviour of the lower classes”
“The One-after-the-One?” Hayley snapped back. “That should not be too hard, but why don’t you put your Level 6 applicant onto it? If he’s such a genius it won’t take long.”
“A challenge? Perhaps you do not think you can do it yourself?” 
“Do not try such pitiful mind games, you insult me and demean yourself.” She wasn’t going to suck his dick to get the job, that was for certain.
“Ha! Okay, perhaps we might have ourselves a contest!” The CEO was intrigued. What mischief will unfold if I agree? “How about a direct competition? Whomsoever finds the One-after-the-One shall be the Commissioner.” 
“That’s not what I had in mind, sir.” Hayley managed to sputter. What just happened? Shit!. “And when I find him? What shall we do with him?”
“He or she will be killed, of course. This impostor is a symbol of hope. HOPE!!” The CEO raised the volume. “Hope is something no-one, no low, is permitted to hold or even to crave. They must learn that hope melts away as soon as their grimy hands grasp it. ”
“How do you propose to arrange this little grudge match?” Hayley asked gingerly, hoping the CEO saw the absurdity of the suggestion.
“Well ,I will swear him in as a Chief Superintendent and give him access to the same resources you have. After that it’s up to you two. In fact, why don’t you two meet and work it out? The CEO smiled and waved his hand over the console on his desk and the holographic head of his personal assistant was immediately floating in front of him. “Darlene. Could you please contact our level 6 applicant? And get him into my office?”
“Yes, sir.” She replied. “It should not be more that 5 minutes. He has just finished the medical.” The floating head popped out of existence.
“You can wait a couple of minutes, can’t you Hayley?”
“Why not?” She said. “I am interested to find out why a person of his stature would want to be in the public service.”
“I think he will peak more than just your interest.” The CEO said. This ought to be fucking interesting. 
After only a few moments of excruciating silence, the hologram of Darlene again made an appearance, “Sir, he’s here.”
“Well, let him in” The said the CEO as the double doors of leading to his outer office slowly opened. “Detective Chief Superintendent Hayley Lanning, I think you know Haloren Smythe, Director, L6.” The recently released accused mass murderer entered the office.
“He is the applicant? A serial killer?” Hayley groaned loudly. “This is your front-runner? A murderer!”
“Now, now. The prosecution service had to drop the case, it seems someone leaked the arrest video to the media. Did you ever find out who leaked it?”
“No, we did not.” Hayley said, keeping a lid on her desire to scream. “That should not effect the court case, there is more than enough evidence. We have a recorded confession.”
“Not good enough!” The CEO snapped. “You thought you could sink a level six with a lousy confession? Not nearly good enough.”
“I told you what would happen to me if you brought me in.” Haloren said. “You should have killed me when you had the chance.”
“My integrity is worth more that some petty act of vengeance.”
“That is you tragic flaw, Chief Superintendent.” The CEO chimed in. “You are inflexible and the upper executive class need a Commissioner who is entirely more pliable.”
“You want a crook.”
“Now you are getting it.” The CEO grinned as he turned to Smythe. “Haloren, the Chief Superintendent here has proposed something marvelous. A contest!” 
* * **************************************************************
“Haloren Smythe?” Sarah asked incredulously. “You are in a contest with a serial killer to find and execute my son?” 
“A serial killer with the resources and investigative capability of the entire P.T.D. Police department.” Halyley quipped. “Trust me, he will find Richard.”
“How is it that you went to that meeting as the Commissioner-in-waiting and end up drawing straws to kill Richard?” 
“It was certainly an unexpected turn of events. I challenged his ability to conduct a criminal investigation and the CEO just ran with it.” Hayley knew she had planted the idea in he head but decided, quite correctly, Sarah would not be impressed. “The next thing I knew I was in a contest. I could not pull out, I would have lost the Commissioner’s job on the spot.”
“I would hate the welfare of my son to get in the way on your career.”
“If I had withdrawn from the contest, do you think they would have stopped looking for Richard?”
“No, of course not.” Sarah conceded. “The danger to Richard seemed distant and intangible until you put a name to it. Haloren Smythe. No matter what, we protect Richard at all costs. Agreed?”
“Do you really need to ask?” Hayley was a little hurt. “I will protect Richard with my last breath. I have seen what he can do. He is special, very special indeed.”
“The Elvi will need to be informed.” Sarah said, her brain now lit up, formulating the seed of a plan. “Yes, we will need the Elvi and all the money in the world.”
“All the money in the world?” Hayley asked.
“Not all, obviously, but most of it.” Sarah forced a smug grin. 

- - -


— - — - - - - - - - - - - - - - — - - - 
The planned genocide of the Elvi had not been stopped, but had by necessity re-organised, prioritising the manufacture of deadly micro-organisms. Stocks of viable virus were replenished and the program was back on track within two months. The wounds of the condemned Elvis prisoners had healed and they had regained their resolve. Each were held in isolation, ignorant of the other’s fate, but knowing none would ever betray their brothers and sisters. 
In the first isolation chamber Elvis was strapped to an interrogation chair, gagged and blindfolded. Electrodes and a tangle of wires attached him to a jumble of medical devices and machines haphazardly assembled around him. His breathing remained slow and regular, the heart monitor beeped, sounding out the cadence of dignified calm. The gaping sore that had taken the place of his ear had been proficiently tended to and was healing, albeit slowly. 
“We are going to test a viral agent on you Mr Elvis. It is expected that you will die.” Dr…… said with a smile. “I am going to take off your blindfold and gag. Please don’t yell or scream. It will do you no good and only serve to annoy.” 
“I have no reason to scream” Elvis said. “You do not frighten me. You do not frighten any of us. Libera Elvi Superbia! ”
“What is that supposed to mean?”
“Deliver Elvi Freedom!”
“No, I think you guys should brush up on you Latin.” Dr ???? corrected. “I will be injecting the viral agent and the effects should be immediate.” The doctor approached with an old-style syringe and needle and making no attempt to locate a blood vessel, plunged it into subcutaneous tissue of the neck and forcefully pressed the plunger.
The pain was instantaneous and excruciating, but the Elvis did not blink or even contort his face, but the heart monitor began beeping faster and faster and yet faster again. His breathing became laboured and he coughed violently as his organs began to bleed out. In less that five minutes the Elvis was dead, drowned in his own fluids, blood and snot foaming from nose and mouth.
“Well that was successful, but injection is a very inefficient delivery system.” Dr &gt;??? Said to his colleagues. “We will have to weaponise the agent. Atomised liquid or powder?” 
“Atomising the virus should be quicker, but less efficient than concentrated airborne powder.” Dr&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; replied. “I can work on the liquid version of the agent and you can get onto reducing it to powder.”
“We are yet to work out the dosage. Clearly we gave our subject far more that actually needed to ensure death. Let’s write this up and get onto the final phase of development.” 
“Keep the body on ice. Director Hardman wants to send the Elvi a message.” 
_ - - - - - - - - - — - - - - - - - - — - -
The battered bodies of 5 deceased Elvi, missing one ear a piece, were found in the street adjacent to the Elvi Parliament Building in the Quarter, each hung by the neck, with thick hemp rope, in a post-mortem lynching. The outcry of those unfortunate enough to stumble across the outrage drew out thousands more from their slumber, into the street, to join the Elvi ebullition. As the lamentations increased louder and louder, the crowd of mourners grew exponentially into a throng of many thousand, their loss soon morphing into rage.
“My Elvi brothers and Sisters, this atrocity will not go unpunished.” The High Elvis addressed the angry mob. He was just as incensed as the rest, but wanted to ensure a riot and bloodbath would not ensue. “Lynching the Elvi is a mistake the P.T.D will regret, I promise you, but this shocking scene has been deliberately staged to anger us into acting out. We cannot allow the Anti-Elvi forces to set our agenda. We cannot allow our uncontrolled anger to seal our fate. We all know of the threat the P.T.D. poses to the very existence of our Elvis society and they only need an excuse to come into the Quarter and destroy us. We must be smarter than that, we must endure this pain in order to deliver retribution.”
“They must all die!” Shouted an Elvis from among the mourners. Many an Elvi agreed enthusiastically calling out “Yeah, Yeah” which quickly descended into “Kill them all, kill them all!”
“Yes, but we must first discover who “they” are.” The High Elvis said, desperately hoping he may be able to talk the mob down. “We will not strike out blindly in all directions, caring not who we harm. That is something the P.T.D. elite would do. That is not the way of Elvis. We will find out who did this and we will act decisively. I will bring them before you to do as you think fit.”
The mourners met the resolve of the High Elvis with a great cheer, knowing that their blood-lust would be satiated and the perpetrators would come to understand the monumental error they had made in rousing the ire of the Elvi.

____ - - - - - - - — — - - - - - - - - — - - - — 
Cracker was glad to see Sarah, but was surprised to see Alex by their side but motioned them into the lounge area of the vast apartment. “What brings you here?” 
“I need access to the finance data base and I need Alex to be there.”
“He knows about it?”
“Yes, I need him to contact his mother at precisely the right moment.” Sarah said.
“Great. Did you tell anyone else?” Cracker replied.
“No. Trust me on this one, I need to cement her as an ally.” Sarah face was blank, but Richard grasped his own hands with fingers interlocked and silently pleaded.
“It’s not as if I can say no, certainly not to Richard.” Cracker smiled at a laughing Richard who unclasped his hand clapped and kicked his legs wildly.
“Okay, let’s do this thing.” Sarah said as she left the room and paced with purpose toward the entry to the control room, Richard giggling as he bounced on her hip. 
“After you, Alex.”
“This is a really lovely apartment. What area are we in?”
“You don’t know you where you are?”
“I never take any notice, you know me.” Alex turned and followed after Sarah. 
Sarah was seated at the main console for the control centre and Cracker set to swiping the inside of his cheek with his finger and smearing the ID panel. 
“Blood would have been quicker.” Sarah noted.
“No thanks.” 
After a few minutes the monitors booted up and final security details scrolled up the screen, listing everything identifiable in his saliva. After a long list of bacteria, fruit, various meat-stuffs and narcotics filled the screen, the name Hardy, Jamison 51% + 49% unknown.” Security must have calculated this was close enough and they were granted access. Sarah took the reigns and got to work, stopped once only when she reached some sort of an impasse. Richard grasped a good chunk of her hair and pulled with all his might, stealing her attention away from the screen that refused to give her the answer she wanted. A short glance in his eyes and a bright smile appeared across her face. 
“Of course, you little genius!” Sarah kissed gently on his forehead. “It’s really quite simple when you look at it that way.” Richard giggled as Sarah worked on the old machine. “Okay, I think we are ready. Alex call your mother.”
“Mother? It’s me, Alex.” Shakti stuttered.
“What do you want?”
“I am with Sarah in a giant computer room, but it’s really old. There’s old keyboards and only 2D screens and and Sarah says it’s Jamison Hardy’s old central control room.” Alex waited for a reply. “Hello? Mother?”
“Give hand the device to Sarah, dear.” Eloise mind was spinning. It’s been found!
“Hello, Eloise.” Sarah smiled down the phone. 
“Sarah dear. Listen to me carefully. If you are where you claim to be you will need help gaining access. Security will be tight.”
“We are already in.”
“You don’t know what you are dealing with, very powerful forces. If you interfere with the natural order, economies would be devastated”
“If you have any money in off-shore accounts, investments in finance organisations that cater only to the super-wealthy?” Sarah asked.
“I have heard of these places.”
“Yes, the tax havens. If you do what I say, tomorrow you be considerable more wealthy than you are now.”
“What do you want me to do?”
“It might be a good idea to divest yourself of any off-shore accounts or investments immediately. I am realiably informed about one third of that investment money will become inaccessible for a period of 24 hours.”
“What area of investment will be safe during this period.”
“I would strongly urge you to invest in Elvis Corporation stock.”
“You are kidding.”
“I want you and a all of your richest friends to take out all of your money, all at the same time. If the withdrawals are of sufficient size, you will sett off alarm bells all over the world. I will shut off the flow of money and when others of your ilk try to withdrawal their money, they will get nothing. I expect a run on these banks and huge losses and by the time the tap is turned some will already be closed.”
“Why Elvis?”
“For what I have in mind, Elvis stocks will be safe. You will get get make your friends rich and enemies poor, depending on who you choose to tell. We will send a message to the most powerful. That we can get them where it hurts.”
“For what purpose?” Eloise said, horrified by the audacity.”
“It is just a demonstration. Most investors will only be moderately inconvenienced. Some of course, those already on the edge, may not survive even one day without liquidity. The CEO must be replaced or further demonstrations will be made. I may not be so charatible as to give you forewarning next time. You and your friend’s will make sure he goes down. Richard is in mortal danger if our current CEO stays in place.” 
“When? Will this happen?”
“We are ready right now. Make your calls you have one hour. The people you save will owe you for life.” The clock had started ticking. 
“We will not want stock, just our money and a reasonable return on the investment, say 5%?” 
“For one day? 1%”
“I thought you might fall for that one. 2%”
“At 100% per annum it is less a than 0.3% for a day. How about 1.5%?”
“You drive a hard bargain, but I am feeling charitable. No shares, just a loan 1.5% for one day. How much can you handle?”
“Whatever you got.” 
Immediate response to the massive transfer of funds from some of the biggest players on the planet did not go unnoticed. Obviously there was something amiss with the upper-tier banking system and everyone wanted out. Thousands of withdrawals were denied. The banks could not meeting the demand, their leverage ratios were way too high and they many ceased trading for the day. The stock market, always looking for a good reason to plummet vertical, panicked and shrank like an erection room with a vomiting fat chick.
A large chuck of the backroom cash had stopped moving and no amount of manipulating the system seemed to clear the log-jam. It could not just disappear, but that did not stop half the world grinding to a halt when money slowed to a trickle. No-one knew where the money lay. Somewhere in the system most would surmise, hoping it would reset and all would be well, but it was impossible to know when it may happen and they all had to assume they had just driven off a cliff. Bridging finance was immediately scarce, except for the loans offered from the good people at Elvis Corporation Savings and Loans. They seemed to have plenty of money to throw around. Using the temporarily quarantined cash, Elvis Corporation Saving and Loans were effectively loaning desperate investors their own money at outrageous interest rates. 
Although the loan scam was lucrative, it was miniscule in comparison to the money Sarah began to throw around. She diverted the balance of the funds into millions of short burst high risk micro-trades, programing the old system to preemptively act, knowing the conditions were temporary and predicting the market a millisecond at a time. Some bets went poorly, but the vast majority were yielded high returns. The amount of money invested in this manner at any given moment could buy a reasonable sized nation-state and the yield, Sarah calculated, would more than cover the loans doled out by Elvis Corp savings and loan. When Sarah turned the tap back on and her ingenuous algorithm had covered it’s tracks, many of the world’s richest people were left with on few lousy million and the Elvis Corporation controlled a decent chunk of the world’s debt. 
“Well dear that worked out well for all of us. I will need my investment back immediately plus my 1.5% interest. I see Elvis Corp has up 500% in one day, I guess I should have bought stock. Property prices have plummeted and I am one of the few with money.” Eloise told Sarah when she called.. “You must come around to my house some time soon. We have much to discuss. No-one should have that much power. Except me.
“Yes, I will pop around with Richard some day soon.”
“Don’t worry he will be safe at my house. It may be one of the safest places for him.”



