        <Document ID="3BF696C0-3871-44A9-B551-56B4640229CC">
            <Title>Eloise Shakti CEO</Title>
            <Text>Eloise Shakti, CEO
“Good morning Eloise.” Sarah greeted on the other end of the vid-phone. 
“Yes, how can I help you?” Eloise said. “As I am a very busy person these days.”
“I wish to arranged a meeting with you today.”
“In regards to what?” Eloise asked.
“The cyber attack upon the financial system of the PTD.” Sarah replied.
“I think we have that matter under control.” Although Eloise was yet to hear from the two privateers she had set upon Cracker she was unconcerned. Wet work of mercenaries could not be hurried or managed with timetables or measured on a clock. These things took as long as they took. She was confident that the level 2 dullard known as Cracker would sell-out all of the Elvi in an instant to save his worthless hide. 
“I would insist we speak.” Sarah pressed, then after some thought added, “Richard would very much like to see you, too.”
“Oh, why didn’t you say?” Eloise voice immediately changed to a bright friendly, pleasant tone. “I always have time for my grandson. I have no meetings between 3 and 4pm today. See you both then.” She terminated the communication.

 - - -
As the meeting with Sarah approached, Eloise still had not heard from her operatives and she was now reasonably sure the mission had failed. Sarah’s overtures for an impromptu family reunion had become increasingly suspicious as the time passed and no word was received. Sarah must about the raid, that much was certain. Machiavellian by choice, Eloise was always prepared for setbacks and had an infinite capacity for thinking on her feet and taking the most aggressive option available. No matter what Sarah had to say, Eloise would have an answer. If that failed, extortion was not beneath her.
 
“Thank you for making the time for Richard and I, Eloise.” Sarah said placing Richard on the floor. 
“Come here my little marvel.” Eloise bent down, arms out, awaiting the familiar crash of Richard gleefully running into her embrace, but Richard remained stationary, a look of disdain across his little face. “What’s wrong, little man?”
“You tried to kill, Cracker. Grandmother.” Richard said slowly.
“What?” Eloise was in shock. “He speaks!”
“Yes, I do Grand-mama.” Richard confirmed.
“And with an English accent, no less!” Eliose replied. “Received pronunciation accent, it is not?”
‘Yes, grand-mama.” Richard said, “It is not by choice. This body speaks this way.” 
“We are here to discuss why you would send goons to rough up, Cracker.” Sarah interjected. As interesting as she found the discussion, she thought they should get to the business at hand. 
“Oh, Sarah, my daughter-in-law, why do you care for the fate of such a low-life?” Eloise was genuinely perplexed. “He is nothing, an uneducated orphan with no prospects.”
“He is the only living beneficiary to the Hardy fortune.” Sarah countered. “He will be the richest person who ever lived. Doesn’t that count as prospects?”
“Bah! Any claim to the Hardy fortune will be blocked in the courts and I will ensure he is stuck in litigation for years, decades if necessary. He will never inherit anything.” Eloise decreed. “N.O.O.C. darling - Not of our class. He will not inherit credit one.”
“Grand-mama, you are wrong.” Richard countered.
“Well it seems we are going to have to teach you some manners, young man.” 
“No, you must learn.” Richard eyes met with Eloise. “Class structures do not promote the evolution of the individual, it crushes the majority for the benefit of the few.”
“Oh dear! A lib-tard lefty!” Eloise rolled her eyes, genuinely frustrated. “You have a lot a growing up to do.” She laughed, just a little, at the picture of her telling a toddler he has a lot of growing up to do. “Sarah? What have you been teaching my grandson?”
“I learn myself.” Richard protests.
“We are not here for a debate on the merits of our social structures.” Sarah again tried to get the conversation back on track. “What did you think you were doing sending those men to obtain access to the Hardy finance data base.”
“Simple, my dear.” Eloise smiled widely. “I wish to take control of the system for the benefit of the PTD.”
“Altruism from you?” Sarah giggled at the absurdity. Eloise-the-atruistic? “I think you may have your own welfare in mind.”
“Of course” Eloise admitted. “Benevolence gets you nowhere, you know that. It is just that I cannot allow that Cracker person to have access to such an important and dangerous resource.”
“It is not your property and it is not up to you.”
“The existence of Jamison Hardy’s finance system is a clear and present danger to the financial health of our Dominion. I am the CEO and the PTD has suffered an attack. I cannot allow a repeat.”
“You personally benefited from the ‘attack’ as you call it.” Sarah pointed out. “I did not have to let you in on it. You could have suffered like the rest, but I did not let that happen.” 
“Had you not, dear, this conversation would have been very different.” Eloise warned.
“I figured that, but it was my expectation you would display something similar to gratitude.” Sarah replied. “It does not seem unreasonable.”
“I decide what is reasonable!” Eloise raised her voice, her eyes wide and wild. “I am the CEO, I decide what will and what will not happen in the PTD. You may have your expectations, but I have my duty and I must protect the economic interest of the dominion. Family, friends and old associations are secondary considerations.”
“Thank you, Grand-mama.” Richard interrupted. “I think mother will agree that there is now no chance of you being granted access.”
“Is that right, my little grandson?” Eloise smiled, turning to Sarah she continued, “Some disturbing information has crossed my desk over the past few days. It would seem our illustrious Police Commissioner is also a revered religious figure of the Elvi Nation. A religious figure! And it is suspected she has acted against the interests of the PTD, on behalf of the Elvi.” 
“Don’t be ridiculous.” Sarah replied. “As sad as it is, she’s 100% cop.”
 
“Mind your words young lady.” Eloise warned Sarah for the second time. “There are rumours spreading that not only was she behind the Black Monday cyber-attack, she has a clandestine operation underway on the outskirts of town. Some say she is cooking up a weapon of some sort.”
“You know she wasn’t behind the cyber attack and I understand police operations are sometimes clandestine.” Sarah was a little rattled, security around the operation is water tight…..oh shit, Shakti! 
“Details like that do not matter.” Eloise volleyed back.
“Details? Like the truth?” Sarah incredulous.
“The truth is always a matter of perspective and my truth has the backing of the PTD.” Eloise replied. “The Board of Directors will take the view that she was either involved or she allowed it to happen due to incompetence. Either way, her position as Commissioner is shaky at best.”
“You cannot afford to lose such a dedicated officer!” Sarah pleaded in high voice. 
“Dedicated?” Eloise face screwed-up. “Was it dedication on display when she took the title of Holy Aunt Hayley?”
“The Elvi call me Blessed Mother. It means nothing apart from, perhaps, respect.” Sarah explained. “I did not, nor did Hayley, ask for respect or reverence from the Elvi. Quite the opposite in fact.”
“It matters not. Hayley cannot be both Commissioner and Holy Icon and since she has not control over whether she is a Holy Icon,, she cannot be the Commissioner.” Eloise said. “I will be asking for her resignation and if that is not forthcoming her contract will be terminated, along with her.”
“That is evil.” Richard said quietly.
“Or I can be granted access to the system.” Eloise said, smile radiating white.
“I will speak with Hayley and get back to you.” Sarah said, her eye unable to meet Eloise’s gaze.
“Good. I expect an answer by the end of the week.” Eloise said at speed. “Now, Richard are you going to give Grand-mama a hug?”
“Yes.” Richard hugged her as hard he could and with his mouth to her ear whispered, “Please don’t hurt my friends Grand-mama. I need them for what is to come.”
“It’s just business, Richard. You will understand when you are older.” Eloise lifted Richard to the waiting arms of Sarah.
“This is a terrible business.” Sarah terminated the conversation and took Richard out the door.
 - - -
“ 


		The work on the disc will proceed to the point that they have decoded a few messages - 
		Mostly desperate pleas or recording the entire aggregate knowledge of the civilization. (Music, Art, history, science, memes - everything ever recorded.
		The “other” earths are almost exactly the same, some divergence in political landscapes, names of countries (USA = UACS) (PTD = Eastern Australia) (Vietnesia = China) and leaders (Trump = Dunning Kruger), but fundamentally similar.
		With the exception of their own earth which is different is a few fundamental ways 
		All other earths only have one Elvis who had a stellar albiet short career. (Compare names of songs Kentucky Rain? Love me Tender? (The High Elvis will not be impressed and will ridicule the lack of science and reason in the songs - No songs about evolution? What was he thinking? And those Elvis movies are just awful - I would never stoop so low.)
		There is no equivalent Richard Dawkins clone at the time of the crunch, but some of the other players are represented in the other universes - Sarah, Johnny, CEO (Prime Minister), Hayley, Damien Hardman and on each and every occasion, no matter what they did, they could not stop the universe from collapsing in on itself. (Alway preceded by o the discovery of the gyges discs) The PTD universe is different and they have a degree of hope that they may be able to stop the cycle of universes being destroyed and other universes popping into existence.
		It would seem that the conditions precedent for the end of the universe -Discovery of the disks once the disks are discovered/created annihilation is inevitable. All who have tried to stop the inevitability have failed. But they have the Dawkins and the Elvi Nation.
		Initial attempts to download the information, crashes the computer capacity of the lab and the information was lost. The information is dumped at once, sort of a zip file with the information enclosed in packets of data once opened.
		Have to use the quatum bio-processors of the Hardy control centre as they have the capacity to handle the data, but the memory of the computer has to be all but wiped or transferred to another site.
		For the system to handle the information, Richard has to act as a biological buffer for serialising and marshalling the vast information dump.
		Some sort of double dealing with Eloise to use her computers to dump the finance database to her computers. She will think she has got control, but when she tries to fire it up, she will discover that she cannot open the system without DNA key code. 
		When the transfer happens Richard will be wired to the system with from various contact points on his head.He tells them not to stop the transfer no matter what. Stopping mid stream could pop him out of existence or he could possibly jump time lines. The transfer is slow at first and then he begins to glow, low at first, but as he glows brighter the data transfer rate increases and he glows brighter and brighter. Gravity seems to increase and the become heavier and heavier. Furniture begins to buckle and squish diagonally down towards the bunker. They all begin to freak out and big debate as to whether to stop. Eventually Johnny tries and fighting against the gravity he almost hits the “stop” button - somehow thwarted.
		Richard finally glows less and less until you can see him - a grown man in his mid 20’s. Due to time dilation it was only 10minutes for the occupants of the bunker but 20 years for Richard. Q’s about how? “My brain had to grow (evolve) to cope with the data and the nature of the gravity well slowed down time for him and he had time to process the information. He 
		When the fridge guys arrive they are aghast. “Do you know what could have happened if you spin the dics? You could have collapsed the entire universe. How It did not happen is impossible!” “Maybe we are all dead” said Cracker. Richard, now a full grown adult confirms Cracker’s idea of inoculating one with the Panacea virus and one with the Panacea Anti-virus proves to be correct and the transfer is successful. 
		Johnny gets dealt with - no acknowledgement of any part of the discovery of multi-verses (or a series of big-bang/big crunch universes)
		The information is vast but all earths end the same way. The discovery of the discs always precede the eventual demise of the universe, just the amount of time it takes differs. The player are pretty much the same in the other multi-verses, but in the PTD there is an extra character - The Dawkins - they a are involved with the examination of the discs in the PTD. 
</Text>
