            <Title>Congratulations on your purchase</Title>
            <Synopsis>Basic description of the country known as Ulyssia.  Polluted and barren.</Synopsis>
            <Text> 
Congratulations on purchasing your new Elvis Entertainment and Hospitality Unit.
No matter whether this is your first Elvis, or you have previously leased an Elvis, you’re sure to appreciate the safety, economy and superb engineering of your new Grayling Corporation product. 
In this Warranty and Service Book you’ll find all the information you need to ensure your Elvis is maintained in the best possible condition. You will also find an explanation of everything covered by your 5 year/10,000 hour comprehensive Elvis Entertainment and Hospitality unit warranty.
Nothing helps the resale value of your Elvis like a complete service history from your authorised Elvis Service Centre. It demonstrates to any potential buyer that you’ve taken care of your Elvis, making it an invaluable asset for negotiating the best possible resale price. We suggest you ensure each Elvis keeps this Warranty and Service Booklet on his or her person so your Elvis Service Centre can easily stamp it at every service. The book must be stamped, as electronic records or service invoices are not accepted as evidence of a service.
Your responsibilities
You must operate, maintain and care for your Elvis properly, in accordance with the instructions in this book and your Elvis owner’s manual. The best way to maintain your Elvis through an authorised Elvis Service Centre. 
What is not covered by your Elvis Entertainment and hospitality unit
		Clothes, shoes and musical instruments. It is the responsibility of the owner to clothe your Elvis and provide him or her with suitable equipment to carry out their duties.
		Misuse and neglect as defined in the owners-manual.
		Providing insufficient or poor quality housing and food. 
		Feeding after midnight
		Feeding bacon fat and coffee grounds
		Working excessive or lengthy hours without sufficient rest and repose.
		Exposing your Elvis to amphetamine, crystal methamphetamine, cocaine, ‘crack’ cocaine or any other stimulant drug or drug patch.
		Exposing the Elvis to religion or religious memes/icons including religious texts, psalms, hymns, gospel music or revelation of any kind. 
		Accident damage.
		Choking on or inhaling rhinestones.
		With the exception of the free 100hr service – medical and dental costs.
  </Text>
