            <Title>Halo meets Avi</Title>
            <Text>After Sarah disappeared with Cracker, Halo skulled the last of his schooner, and allowed his anger to dissipate through his fingers and toes. Then he saw a new target on the far side of the bar. She looked out of place, neither a punter nor a staff member. She moved with a certain detachment to people and things around her. She spoke to no one. She appeared to be alone. It wasn’t until he stole by her side, he could see how dilated her pupils were, how flush and dimpled her skin, how deeply and evenly she breathed. She was already aroused, perhaps from playing a fantasy in her head, or because she had some exotic fetish. Maybe the smell of stale beer, who could say? If Halo could say, he’d say she liked to finish off the way he liked, though such would be foolhardy in the environs of a bar. When she sensed his presence and locked eyes with him, she surrendered to her desire, gave her mouth and tongue to him, yielded her pelvis to grind his, raised her arms to enwrap him. She clasped his hand with gentle promise and took him outside. He felt like a warrior as he pushed her against wall in a side alley, and spent a small fraction of his lust gaining access to coy parts of her body. She made whatever he sought available as she unbuttoned his pants.
He smiled as he thought of this one and Sarah as a composite, as a conglomerate conquest. Sarah could wait. He’d get to her after Cracker inevitably failed. He’d preserved his averages, his track record, after all. He knew Sarah’s type: an Airborne who toyed with Cloudborne for sport. He admired that in her.
With their hands occupied, Halo and the new girl locked mouths in an extended vacuum-inducing kiss.
Then their lust exploded and knocked them over.
“Wow that was some kiss,” Halo said, thus proving he had a sense of humour. He was very satisfied with himself.
The girl was orgasming. “I come so hard when I blow things up,” she said hoarsely into his ear. She had no fear of making such a confession, not with the plans she had.
Halo noticed there was dust caking in her hair. His mouth was filling with it, and he coughed hard.
People had been shouting, and screaming, and wailing. There was whimpering. Halo knew the quality of the whimpers: the sounds of the dying giving up. All these sounds were around him, only gradually invading his self-obsessed narrative.
The street was filling with people, survivors of the blast and gawkers.
“We must leave,” she said, and put his throbber back in his pants, giving it a pat through his underwear.

Her quarters were not too far. On the way, Halo learned her name was Avi, but nothing else, other than, “We should hurry.”
They hurried into her quarters, a very small studio but neat and clean. They hurried to her mattress and hurried to scatter dust from the explosion on her burgundy sheets. They hurried through the foreplay. She was confident, and led for much of the time. He allowed her on top. When he asserted, she became compliant. She joyfully took all of him in her mouth and kept him all the way down in her throat while she worked her lips and teeth and tongue around him. She squeezed his sack and almost triggered his point of no return, so he withdrew, turned her over and brought her up on her knees. After a few well-considered, artful strokes, he went in deep and fully. She made noises into the pillow, and pressed a hand under it for leverage while she reached back to rub her clit. Their bodies slapped together. Balls and tits swung vigorously and rhythmically.
Halo increased the strength of his strokes, thumping Avi’s head into the wall. Her fingers left her clit to its own engorgement, and sought out her favorite sex toy. She loved it more, even, than home-made explosives. It was her particle pistol. “Pound me!” she grunted. You will shortly be dead, so service me while you can.
Halo’s hand snaked to his jacket on the end of the mattress, and drew out his own favorite sex toy: a small, glistening three-sided stainless steel spike, the Slice of Life. Of his own design, it tapered from a grip in the middle to sharp points at both ends. It left a savage, gaping wound that—if Halo nailed the entry properly—would gush like a fountain through its bored-out, end-to-end hollow centre. He liked it. He liked it a lot.
Here we approach the discovery of what happens when two serial killers make the beast of conjoined sex organs, the inevitability of two lying down, and only one standing up. Who would it be? Would each wait for the other to come? How many premature shooters had Avi shot? Would she savour the feeling of Halo’s semen gumming up her rectal cavity as he breathed his last? How, exactly, does the ejaculating penis of a dying man behave? Could there be a more fundamental existential question? And what of Halo? Would he wait for her to squirt, or do whatever women do when they fake it these days? Would her climax (if she had one) produce a more satisfying fountain of blood from the wound? Or would her kill her as he reached his point of no return, so she expired as he popped?
Avi had well-placed mirrors in the corners of the studio. As Halo played the beast, he made poses and examined himself in each mirror. He examined the Slice of Life in his hand from every angle. Halo’s vanity could be his downfall; he failed to notice Avi’s toy emerging from under the pillow.
Avi dropped out of doggy position, popping Halo from inside her, and twisted round to aim the pistol. Halo’s eye’s widened.
The truth of it is, the movements Avi needed to kill Halo were less economical than the movements he needed to kill her. He pressed a knee into her shoulder blade, flattening her on the mattress. The pistol came free from her hand, but even if she held it, she would never be able to accurately aim. Halo had an open, point-blank target. He plunged the spike into Avi’s back, splintering her spine, separating ribs and annihilating her heart. Death took her quickly, but her blood did not gush, as Halo required. There were a few final pathetic flutters. There was no cathartic last gasp for breath. Halo was deflated. A hit to the lungs should, at the very least, produce bright pink foam from the wound and the corner her mouth. He’d planned to stab her in the neck—it was entirely more graphic—but he’d rushed it when he saw the pistol coming up.
Needing consolation, he pulled the body on its knees and reamed it. Finishing off didn’t make him feel any better, it made him angry. And bitter. Some people didn’t know how to die according to his needs.
Halo took a closer look at the gun. Agency issue, only covert agents carried particle pistols. Tax! Avi may have been serious. I come so hard when I blow things up. She had been out on an operation, and he’d killed her. He paled with shock. His cock shrivelled to a peanut. How could he possibly know an operative would have a job in the Stick It Inn? Who or what did they want to hit in there? Was he the target, and Avi was on a need-to-know about the details? Was someone onto his extra-curricular slices of life?
Avi would be missed. Someone might actually investigate her death. His MO was hit targets no one would miss. This time, he’d let that Sarah cloud his judgment. He might have only a few hours before anyone would be looking for Avi. He had to clean the studio, professionally.
But first, he’d needed to conquer his fury. He ransacked the place, looking for clues he might exploit. Then, he needed to go out and find a do-over.
</Text>
