        <Document ID="C8C1A0EF-746C-4C97-AC38-8D7E0AC2C82A">
            <Title>Cracker</Title>
            <Text>Anthony “Cracker” Hardy
		Role in Story:		Central Male Character
		Occupation:		Contract Cleaner 
   	
		Physical Description:	Eurasian appearance, 183cm, medium build, dark straight hair, pale complexion, dark slightly hooded eyes, 			straight-slender nose, bright smile with straight white teeth. Hands calloused, cracked and grimy. 
		Personality:	Poorly educated, but intelligent, street-wise and wise cracking. He has a childish and crude sense of humour and regularly makes coarse and inappropriate comments. He will steal anything if there is a prospect of getting away with it, but he is fiercely loyal and would never double-cross a friend. Blend of amoral criminality and Victorian decency.
		Habits/Mannerisms:	Thief, crude comments, attempts at humour. High fives at the wrong time.
    	
		Background:	He was brought up by an uncle who disappeared/abandoned him while he was in his mid teens. He remained in the apartment he was brought up in, expecting eviction that never came. 
		Internal Conflicts:	He hates his station in life and knows he cannot change it. He desperately wants to be loved, but the impersonal nature of the society has made a search for love impossible. He desires women that are higher born and completely out of reach.
		External Conflicts:	 	
    	
		Notes:	</Text>
        </Document>
