        <Document ID="BDFC475A-DAD1-4150-BC93-50C51C954120">
            <Title>D-sup protien</Title>
            <Text>De Sup protein
Protect against radiation - prevents the radiation from snapping apart.
If the D-sup protein could be transferred to human DNA.




Unique DNA-associating protein that contributes to the exceptional tolerance to harsh environmental stresses (PubMed:27649274). Suppresses X-ray-induced DNA damage including single-strand breaks (SSBs) as well as more hazardous double-strand breaks (DSBs) and improves radiotolerance (PubMed:27649274). Shields also DNA against reactive oxygene species (ROS) (PubMed:27649274).1 Publication
&lt; p&gt;Manually curated information for which there is published experimental evidence.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="/manual/evidences#ECO:0000269"&gt;More…&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; Manual assertion based on experiment ini
		Ref.1
"Extremotolerant tardigrade genome and improved radiotolerance of human cultured cells by tardigrade-unique protein." Hashimoto T., Horikawa D.D., Saito Y., Kuwahara H., Kozuka-Hata H., Shin-I T., Minakuchi Y., Ohishi K., Motoyama A., Aizu T., Enomoto A., Kondo K., Tanaka S., Hara Y., Koshikawa S., Sagara H., Miura T., Yokobori S. 
, Miyagawa K., Suzuki Y., Kubo T., Oyama M., Kohara Y., Fujiyama A., Arakawa K., Katayama T., Toyoda A., Kunieda T. Nat. Commun. 7:12808-12808(2016) [PubMed] [Europe PMC] [Abstract]
Cited for: NUCLEOTIDE SEQUENCE [LARGE SCALE GENOMIC DNA / MRNA], IDENTIFICATION BY MASS SPECTROMETRY,
 SUBCELLULAR LOCATION, DNA-BINDING, FUNCTION.

